 know three 1st-level wizard spells of your choice, two of which you must choose from the abjuration and evocation spells on the wizard spell list.\n\nThe Spells Known column of the Eldritch Knight Spellcasting table shows when you learn more wizard spells of 1st level or higher. Each of these spells must be an abjuration or evocation spell of your choice, and must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For instance, when you reach 7th level in this class, you can learn one new spell of 1st or 2nd level.\n\nThe spells you learn at 8th, 14th, and 20th level can come from any school of magic.\n\nWhenever you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of the wizard spells you know with another spell of your choice from the wizard spell list. The new spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots, and it must be an abjuration or evocation spell, unless you're replacing the spell you gained at 3rd, 8th, 14th, or 20th level from any school of magic.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your wizard spells, since you learn your spells through study and memorization. You use your Intelligence whenever a spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Intelligence modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a wizard spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.\n\nSpell\n\nSpell\n\nNivel 3 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 96\n\nYou have learned to cast spells. See XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules as an Eldritch Knight.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know two cantrips of your choice from the spells (see that class's section for its list). XPHB and XPHB are recommended. Whenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the spells.\n\nWhen you reach Fighter level 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip of your choice.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Eldritch Knight Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 spells from the spells. XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Fighter levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Eldritch Knight Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Fighter, your list of prepared spells can include five Wizard spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.\n\nChanging your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Wizard spell for which you have spell slots.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your Wizard spells.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an XPHB as a XPHB for your Wizard spells.\n\nNivel 3 - War Bond\n\nPagina: 98\n\nYou learn a ritual that creates a magical bond between yourself and one weapon. You perform the ritual over the course of 1 hour, which can be done during a XPHB. The weapon must be within your reach throughout the ritual, at the conclusion of which you touch the weapon and forge the bond. The bond fails if another Fighter is bonded to the weapon or if the weapon is a magic item to which someone else is attuned.\n\nOnce you have bonded a weapon to yourself, you can't be disarmed of that weapon unless you have the XPHB condition. If it is on the same plane of existence, you can summon that weapon as a XPHB, causing it to teleport instantly to your hand.\n\nYou can have up to two bonded weapons, but you can summon only one at a time with a XPHB. If you attempt to bond with a third weapon, you must break the bond with one of the other two.\n\nNivel 3 - War Bond\n\nNivel 3 - Weapon Bond\n\nPagina: 74\n\nAt 3rd level, you learn a ritual that creates a magical bond between yourself and one weapon. You perform the ritual over the course of 1 hour, which can be done during a short rest. The weapon must be within your reach throughout the ritual, at the conclusion of which you touch the weapon and forge the bond.\n\nOnce you have bonded a weapon to yourself, you can't be disarmed of that weapon unless you are incapacitated. If it is on the same plane of existence, you can summon that weapon as a bonus action on your turn, causing it to teleport instantly to your hand.\n\nYou can have up to two bonded weapons, but can summon only one at a time with your bonus action. If you attempt to bond with a third weapon, you must break the bond with one of the other two.\n\nNivel 7 - War Magic\n\nPagina: 74\n\nBeginning at 7th level, when you use your action to cast a cantrip, you can make one weapon attack as a bonus action.\n\nNivel 7 - War Magic\n\nPagina: 98\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action on your turn, you can replace one of the attacks with a casting of one of your Wizard cantrips that has a casting time of an action.\n\nNivel 10 - Eldritch Strike\n\nPagina: 74\n\nAt 10th level, you learn how to make your weapon strikes undercut a creature's resistance to your spells. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, that creature has disadvantage on the next saving throw it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn.\n\nNivel 10 - Eldritch Strike\n\nPagina: 98\n\nYou learn how to make your weapon strikes undercut a creature's ability to withstand your spells. When you hit a creature with an attack using a weapon, that creature has XPHB on the next saving throw it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn.\n\nNivel 15 - Arcane Charge\n\nPagina: 74\n\nAt 15th level, you gain the ability to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see when you use your Action Surge. You can teleport before or after the additional action.\n\nNivel 15 - Arcane Charge\n\nPagina: 98\n\nWhen you use your Action Surge, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. You can teleport before or after the additional action.\n\nNivel 15 - Arcane Charge\n\nNivel 18 - Improved War Magic\n\nPagina: 74\n\nStarting at 18th level, when you use your action to cast a spell, you can make one weapon attack as a bonus action.\n\nNivel 18 - Improved War Magic\n\nPagina: 98\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action on your turn, you can replace two of the attacks with a casting of one of your level 1 or level 2 Wizard spells that has a casting time of an action."},
  ["feature.eldritch-knight.xphb2024.fighter.eldritch-knight.3"]={title="Eldritch Knight",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 96\n\nSupport Combat Skills with Arcane Magic\n\nEldritch Knights combine the martial mastery common to all Fighters with a careful study of magic. Their spells both complement and extend their combat skills, providing additional protection to shore up their armor and also allowing them to engage many foes at once with explosive magic."},
  ["creature.eldritch-lich.mcv1sc2014"]={title="Eldritch Lich",subtitle="Criatura - MCV1SC - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 165 (22d8 + 66)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFar Realm Parasite\n\nInside the lich's torso dwells a wormlike parasite that contains the lich's soul. When the lich dies, it implodes into the parasite, which then vanishes into the Far Realm. In 2d4 days, the parasite causes the lich to reappear within 1d4 miles of where it died. If the lich died inside a magic circle cast to contain Undead, the lich instead reappears as an otyugh with all the lich's memories.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the lich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe lich doesn't need air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe lich makes one Parasitic Tentacle attack or uses Spellcasting. The lich also uses Psychic Whisper twice.\n\nParasitic Tentacle\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h25 (6d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 25 (6d6 + 4) necrotic damage. The target must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned. The poisoned target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The third time the target fails the save, the target dies and dissolves into a gibbering mouther that obeys the lich and uses the target's initiative.\n\nPsychic Whisper\n\nThe lich targets one creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or take 25 (6d6 + 4) psychic damage and be stunned until the end of the lich's next turn as incomprehensible whispers fill the target's mind.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFar Realm Step\n\nImmediately after taking damage, the lich, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, magically teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["feature.eldritch-master.phb2014.warlock.base.20"]={title="Eldritch Master",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\nAt 20th level, you can draw on your inner reserve of mystical power while entreating your patron to regain expended spell slots. You can spend 1 minute entreating your patron for aid to regain all your expended spell slots from your Pact Magic feature. Once you regain spell slots with this feature, you must finish a long rest before you can do so again."},
  ["feature.eldritch-master.xphb2024.warlock.base.20"]={title="Eldritch Master",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-mind.tce2014"]={title="Eldritch Mind",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 71\n\nYou have advantage on Constitution saving throws that you make to maintain your concentration on a spell."},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-mind.xphb2024"]={title="Eldritch Mind",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nYou have XPHB on Constitution saving throws that you make to maintain XPHB."},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-sight.phb2014"]={title="Eldritch Sight",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou can cast detect magic at will, without expending a spell slot."},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-smite.xge2024"]={title="Eldritch Smite",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 56\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with your pact weapon, you can expend a warlock spell slot to deal an extra 1d8 force damage to the target, plus another 1d8 per level of the spell slot, and you can knock the target prone if it is Huge or smaller."},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-smite.xphb2024"]={title="Eldritch Smite",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with your pact weapon, you can expend a Pact Magic spell slot to deal an extra 1d8 Force damage to the target, plus another 1d8 per level of the spell slot, and you can give the target the XPHB condition if it is Huge or smaller."},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-spear.phb2014"]={title="Eldritch Spear",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nWhen you cast eldritch blast, its range is 300 feet."},
  ["optionalfeature.eldritch-spear.xphb2024"]={title="Eldritch Spear",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nChoose one of your known spells that deals damage and has a range of 10+ feet. When you cast that spell, its range increases by a number of feet equal to 30 times your Warlock level.\n\nRepeatable\n\nYou can gain this invocation more than once. Each time you do so, choose a different eligible cantrip."},
  ["magicitem.eldritch-staff.wbtw2014"]={title="Eldritch Staff",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis staff can be wielded as a magic quarterstaff that grants a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it.\n\nThe staff has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20. On a 1, the staff is destroyed in an otherwise harmless burst of eldritch energy.\n\nEldritch Attack\n\nWhen you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can expend up to 3 of its charges. For each charge you expend, the target takes an extra 1d8 lightning damage.\n\nEldritch Escape\n\nIf you take damage while holding the staff, you can use your reaction to expend 3 of the staff's charges, whereupon you turn invisible and teleport yourself, along with any equipment you are wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space that you can see. You remain invisible until the start of your next turn or until you attack, cast a spell, or deal damage."},
  ["feature.eldritch-strike.phb2014.fighter.eldritch-knight.10"]={title="Eldritch Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\nAt 10th level, you learn how to make your weapon strikes undercut a creature's resistance to your spells. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, that creature has disadvantage on the next saving throw it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn."},
  ["feature.eldritch-strike.xphb2024.fighter.eldritch-knight.10"]={title="Eldritch Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 98\n\nYou learn how to make your weapon strikes undercut a creature's ability to withstand your spells. When you hit a creature with an attack using a weapon, that creature has XPHB on the next saving throw it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn."},
  ["feature.eldritch-versatility.tce2014.warlock.base.4"]={title="Eldritch Versatility",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\n{@i 4th-level warlock tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, representing a change of focus in your occult studies:\n\n• Replace one cantrip you learned from this class's Pact Magic feature with another cantrip from the spells.\n\n• Replace the option you chose for the Pact Boon feature with one of that feature's other options.\n\n• If you're 12th level or higher, replace one spell from your Mystic Arcanum feature with another warlock spell of the same level.\n\nIf this change makes you ineligible for any of your Eldritch Invocations, you must also replace them now, choosing invocations for which you qualify."},
  ["deity.elebrin-liothiel.mtf2014"]={title="Elebrin Liothiel",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["item.electrum-ep.phb2014"]={title="Electrum (ep)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 143\n\nRaridade: none\n\nCommon coins come in several different denominations based on the relative worth of the metal from which they are made. The three most common coins are the gold piece (gp), the silver piece (sp), and the copper piece (cp).\n\nWith one gold piece, a character can buy a belt pouch, 50 feet of good rope, or a goat. A skilled (but not exceptional) artisan can earn one gold piece a day. The gold piece is the standard unit of measure for wealth, even if the coin itself is not commonly used. When merchants discuss deals that involve goods or services worth hundreds or thousands of gold pieces, the transactions don't usually involve the exchange of individual coins. Rather, the gold piece is a standard measure of value, and the actual exchange is in gold bars, letters of credit, or valuable goods.\n\nOne gold piece is worth ten silver pieces, the most prevalent coin among commoners. A silver piece buys a laborer's work for a day, a flask of lamp oil, or a night's rest in a poor inn.\n\nOne silver piece is worth ten copper pieces, which are common among laborers and beggars. A single copper piece buys a candle, a torch, or a piece of chalk.\n\nIn addition, unusual coins made of other precious metals sometimes appear in treasure hoards. The electrum piece (ep) and the platinum piece (pp) originate from fallen empires and lost kingdoms, and they sometimes arouse suspicion and skepticism when used in transactions. An electrum piece is worth five silver pieces, and a platinum piece is worth ten gold pieces.\n\nA standard coin weighs about a third of an ounce, so fifty coins weigh a pound."},
  ["item.electrum-50-zib-coin.ggr2014"]={title="Electrum 50-Zib Coin",subtitle="Item - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["feature.elegant-courtier.xge2024.fighter.samurai.7"]={title="Elegant Courtier",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.elegant-maneuver.xge2024.rogue.swashbuckler.13"]={title="Elegant Maneuver",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 48\n\nStarting at 13th level, you can use a bonus action on your turn to gain advantage on the next Dexterity (Acrobatics) or Strength (Athletics) check you make during the same turn."},
  ["feat.elemental-adept.phb2014"]={title="Elemental Adept",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\nWhen you gain this feat, choose one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder.\n\nSpells you cast ignore resistance to damage of the chosen type. In addition, when you roll damage for a spell you cast that deals damage of that type, you can treat any 1 on a damage die as a 2.\n\nYou can select this feat multiple times. Each time you do so, you must choose a different damage type."},
  ["feat.elemental-adept.xphb2024"]={title="Elemental Adept",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 203\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEnergy Mastery\n\nChoose one of the following damage types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. Spells you cast ignore XPHB to damage of the chosen type. In addition, when you roll damage for a spell you cast that deals damage of that type, you can treat any 1 on a damage die as a 2.\n\nRepeatable\n\nYou can take this feat more than once, but you must choose a different damage type each time for Energy Mastery."},
  ["feature.elemental-affinity.phb2014.sorcerer.draconic.6"]={title="Elemental Affinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you cast a spell that deals damage of the type associated with your draconic ancestry, you can add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell. At the same time, you can spend 1 sorcery point to gain resistance to that damage type for 1 hour."},
  ["feature.elemental-affinity.xphb2024.sorcerer.draconic.6"]={title="Elemental Affinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.elemental-attunement.phb2014"]={title="Elemental Attunement",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\nYou can use your action to briefly control elemental forces within 30 feet of you, causing one of the following effects of your choice:\n\n• Create a harmless, instantaneous sensory effect related to air, earth, fire, or water, such as a shower of sparks, a puff of wind, a spray of light mist, or a gentle rumbling of stone.\n\n• Instantaneously light or snuff out a candle, a torch, or a small campfire.\n\n• Chill or warm up to 1 pound of nonliving material for up to 1 hour.\n\n• Cause earth, fire, water, or mist that can fit within a 1-foot cube to shape itself into a crude form you designate for 1 minute."},
  ["feature.elemental-attunement.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.wu-jen.3"]={title="Elemental Attunement",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nStarting at 3rd level, when a creature's resistance reduces the damage dealt by a psionic discipline of yours, you can spend 1 psi point to cause that use of the discipline to ignore the creature's resistance. You can't spend this point if doing so would increase the discipline's cost above your psi limit."},
  ["feature.elemental-attunement.xphb2024.monk.elements.3"]={title="Elemental Attunement",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.elemental-bane.xge2024"]={title="Elemental Bane",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nChoose one creature you can see within range, and choose one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder. The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or be affected by the spell for its duration. The first time each turn the affected target takes damage of the chosen type, the target takes an extra 2d6 damage of that type. Moreover, the target loses any resistance to that damage type until the spell ends."},
  ["feature.elemental-burst.xphb2024.monk.elements.6"]={title="Elemental Burst",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.elemental-cataclysm.xmm2024"]={title="Elemental Cataclysm",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 111\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 370 (20d20 + 160)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 80, swim: 80\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 19 | CON 27 | INT 9 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial\n\nImunidades: acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEarth Glide\n\nThe cataclysm can burrow through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While doing so, the cataclysm doesn't disturb the material it moves through.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the cataclysm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe cataclysm deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nControl Weather\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cataclysm makes two Elemental Burst attacks.\n\nElemental Burst\n\nm,r 15, reach 30 ft. or range 150 ft. h25 (5d6 + 8) damage of a type chosen by the cataclysm: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder.\n\nCataclysmic Event {@recharge 4}\n\nThe cataclysm creates one of the following effects at random (roll 1d4):\n\n• 1: Clinging Flames dex 23, each creature in a 60-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. actSaveFail 45 (13d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail The target starts XPHB.\n\n• 2: Freezing Waves str 23, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 22 (5d8) Bludgeoning damage plus 22 (5d8) Cold damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail The target's XPHB is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn.\n\n• 3: Raging Storm A storm cloud fills a 60-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the cataclysm can see within 150 feet. The cloud lasts for 1 minute or until the cataclysm uses Cataclysmic Event again. Creatures entirely in the cloud have the XPHB and XPHB conditions and can't cast spells with a Verbal component. dex 23, each creature that enters the cloud for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Lightning damage plus 18 (4d8) Thunder damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n• 4: Swallowing Earth str 23, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB originating from a point on the ground within 150 feet. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) Acid damage, and the target has the XPHB condition and is buried under rubble. A buried target has the XPHB condition, has XPHB, and is suffocating. As an action, a buried creature or another creature within 5 feet of it can make a 18 Strength (XPHB) check. On a successful check, the creature is no longer buried. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nEruption\n\nThe cataclysm makes one Elemental Burst attack.\n\nRumbling Movement\n\nThe cataclysm moves up to its XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB without provoking XPHB. Each creature within 5 feet of the cataclysm as it moves is targeted once by the following effect. con 23. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccessOrFail The cataclysm can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["feature.elemental-cleaver.bgg2014.barbarian.giant.6"]={title="Elemental Cleaver",subtitle="Caracteristica - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\n6th-Level Path of the Giant Feature\n\nYour bond with the elemental might of giants grows, and you learn to infuse weapons with primordial energy.\n\nWhen you enter your rage, you can choose one weapon that you are holding and infuse it with one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, thunder, or lightning. While you wield the infused weapon during your rage, the weapon's damage type changes to the chosen type, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of the chosen type when it hits, and it gains the thrown property, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If you throw the weapon, it reappears in your hand the instant after it hits or misses a target. The infused weapon's benefits are suppressed while a creature other than you wields it.\n\nWhile raging and holding the infused weapon, you can use a bonus action to change the infused weapon's current damage type to another one from the damage type options above."},
  ["creature.elemental-cultist.xmm2024"]={title="Elemental Cultist",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 87\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 135 (18d8 + 54)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 18 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Primordial\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cultist makes three attacks, using Elemental Flail or Elemental Claw in any combination.\n\nElemental Flail\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h25 (6d6 + 4) damage of a type chosen by the cultist: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder.\n\nElemental Claw\n\nr 7, range 120 ft. h22 (4d10) damage of a type chosen by the cultist: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the cultist moves the target up to 10 feet straight toward or away from itself.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nElemental Absorption (1/Day)\n\nactTrigger The cultist takes Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage. actResponse The cultist gives itself XPHB to that instance of damage and gains 10 XPHB."},
  ["feature.elemental-disciplines.phb2014.monk.four-elements.3"]={title="Elemental Disciplines",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.elemental-epitome.xphb2024.monk.elements.17"]={title="Elemental Epitome",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.elemental-essence-shard.tce2014"]={title="Elemental Essence Shard",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis crackling crystal contains the essence of an elemental plane. As an action, you can attach the shard to a Tiny object (such as a weapon or a piece of jewelry) or detach it. It falls off if your attunement to it ends. You can use the shard as a spellcasting focus while you hold or wear it.\n\nRoll a d4 and consult the Elemental Essence Shards table to determine the shard's essence and property. When you use a Metamagic option on a spell while you are holding or wearing the shard, you can use that property.\n\nd4 | Element | Shard\n\n1 | Air | TCE\n\n2 | Earth | TCE\n\n3 | Fire | TCE\n\n4 | Water | TCE"},
  ["magicitem.elemental-essence-shard-air.tce2014"]={title="Elemental Essence Shard (Air)",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis crackling crystal contains the essence of an elemental plane. As an action, you can attach the shard to a Tiny object (such as a weapon or a piece of jewelry) or detach it. It falls off if your attunement to it ends. You can use the shard as a spellcasting focus while you hold or wear it.\n\nWhen you use a Metamagic option on a spell while you are holding or wearing the shard, you can use the following property:\n\nProperty\n\nYou can immediately fly up to 60 feet without provoking opportunity attacks."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-essence-shard-earth.tce2014"]={title="Elemental Essence Shard (Earth)",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis crackling crystal contains the essence of an elemental plane. As an action, you can attach the shard to a Tiny object (such as a weapon or a piece of jewelry) or detach it. It falls off if your attunement to it ends. You can use the shard as a spellcasting focus while you hold or wear it.\n\nWhen you use a Metamagic option on a spell while you are holding or wearing the shard, you can use the following property:\n\nProperty\n\nYou gain resistance to a damage type of your choice until the start of your next turn."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-essence-shard-fire.tce2014"]={title="Elemental Essence Shard (Fire)",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis crackling crystal contains the essence of an elemental plane. As an action, you can attach the shard to a Tiny object (such as a weapon or a piece of jewelry) or detach it. It falls off if your attunement to it ends. You can use the shard as a spellcasting focus while you hold or wear it.\n\nWhen you use a Metamagic option on a spell while you are holding or wearing the shard, you can use the following property:\n\nProperty\n\nOne target of the spell that you can see catches fire. The burning target takes 2d10 fire damage at the start of its next turn, and then the flames go out."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-essence-shard-water.tce2014"]={title="Elemental Essence Shard (Water)",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis crackling crystal contains the essence of an elemental plane. As an action, you can attach the shard to a Tiny object (such as a weapon or a piece of jewelry) or detach it. It falls off if your attunement to it ends. You can use the shard as a spellcasting focus while you hold or wear it.\n\nWhen you use a Metamagic option on a spell while you are holding or wearing the shard, you can use the following property:\n\nProperty\n\nYou create a wave of water that bursts out from you in a 10-foot radius. Each creature of your choice that you can see in that area takes 2d6 cold damage and must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC or be pushed 10 feet away from you and fall prone."},
  ["feat.elemental-familiar.au2014"]={title="Elemental Familiar",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nElemental Energy\n\nYou learn how to imbue your familiar with elemental power. When you cast the XPHB spell, choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage. Your familiar is imbued with this energy until you cast XPHB again, granting it the following benefits:\n\nElemental Resistance\n\nYour familiar has XPHB to the chosen damage type.\n\nEnergy Pulse\n\nAs a XPHB, you command your familiar to unleash a burst of elemental energy. Your familiar must be within 120 feet of you and take a XPHB to unleash this burst. Each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from your familiar makes a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier for the XPHB spell and your XPHB). On a failed save, a creature takes 2d4 damage of the chosen type, and if the creature is Medium or smaller, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["feature.elemental-fury.xphb2024.druid.base.7"]={title="Elemental Fury",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 81\n\nThe might of the elements flows through you. You gain one of the following options of your choice."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-blue-sapphire.dmg2014"]={title="Elemental Gem, Blue Sapphire",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you use an action to break the gem, an air elemental is summoned as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell, and the gem's magic is lost."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-blue-sapphire.xdmg2024"]={title="Elemental Gem, Blue Sapphire",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 257\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you take a XPHB action to break the gem, an XMM is summoned, and the gem ceases to be magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-emerald.dmg2014"]={title="Elemental Gem, Emerald",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you use an action to break the gem, a water elemental is summoned as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell, and the gem's magic is lost."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-emerald.xdmg2024"]={title="Elemental Gem, Emerald",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 257\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you take a XPHB action to break the gem, a XMM is summoned, and the gem ceases to be magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-red-corundum.dmg2014"]={title="Elemental Gem, Red Corundum",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you use an action to break the gem, a fire elemental is summoned as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell, and the gem's magic is lost."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-red-corundum.xdmg2024"]={title="Elemental Gem, Red Corundum",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 257\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you take a XPHB action to break the gem, a XMM is summoned, and the gem ceases to be magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-yellow-diamond.dmg2014"]={title="Elemental Gem, Yellow Diamond",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you use an action to break the gem, an earth elemental is summoned as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell, and the gem's magic is lost."},
  ["magicitem.elemental-gem-yellow-diamond.xdmg2024"]={title="Elemental Gem, Yellow Diamond",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 257\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you take a XPHB action to break the gem, an XMM is summoned, and the gem ceases to be magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB."},
  ["feature.elemental-gift.tce2014.warlock.genie.6"]={title="Elemental Gift",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 73\n\n6th-level Genie feature\n\nYou begin to take on characteristics of your patron's kind. You now have resistance to a damage type determined by your patron's kind: bludgeoning (dao), thunder (djinni), fire (efreeti), or cold (marid).\n\nIn addition, as a bonus action, you can give yourself a flying speed of 30 feet that lasts for 10 minutes, during which you can hover. You can use this bonus action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.elemental-mastery.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.wu-jen.14"]={title="Elemental Mastery",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nStarting at 14th level, if you have resistance to a type of damage, you can spend 2 psi points as a reaction when you take damage of that type to ignore that damage; you gain immunity to that damage type until the end of your next turn."},
  ["feature.elemental-rebuke.frhof2014.paladin.noble-genies.15"]={title="Elemental Rebuke",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nWhen you are hit by an attack roll, you can take a XPHB to halve the attack's damage against yourself (round down) and force the attacker to make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker takes damage equal to 2d10 plus your Charisma modifier of one of the following types (your choice): Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. On a successful save, the attacker takes half as much damage.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feature.elemental-smite.frhof2014.paladin.noble-genies.3"]={title="Elemental Smite",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nImmediately after you cast XPHB, you can expend one use of your Paladin and invoke one of the following effects."},
  ["creature.elemental-spirit.tce2014"]={title="Elemental Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40, burrow: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial, understands the languages you speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous Form (Air, Fire, and Water Only)\n\nThe elemental can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe elemental makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (rounded down).\n\nSlam\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d10 + 4 + summonSpellLevel bludgeoning damage (Air, Earth, and Water only) or fire damage (Fire only)."},
  ["creature.elemental-spirit.xphb2024"]={title="Elemental Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 325\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial, understands the languages you know\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous Form (Air, Fire, and Water Only)\n\nThe spirit can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without it counting as XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spirit makes a number of Slam attacks equal to half this spell's level (round down).\n\nSlam\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d10 + 4 + summonSpellLevel Bludgeoning (Earth only), Cold (Water only), Lightning (Air only), or Fire (Fire only) damage."},
  ["spell.elemental-weapon.phb2014"]={title="Elemental Weapon",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\nA nonmagical weapon you touch becomes a magic weapon. Choose one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder. For the duration, the weapon has a +1 bonus to attack rolls and deals an extra 1d4 damage of the chosen type when it hits."},
  ["spell.elemental-weapon.xphb2024"]={title="Elemental Weapon",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 267\n\nA nonmagical weapon you touch becomes a magic weapon. Choose one of the following damage types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. For the duration, the weapon has a +1 bonus to attack rolls and deals an extra 1d4 damage of the chosen type when it hits."},
  ["feature.elemental-wild-shape.phb2014.druid.moon.10"]={title="Elemental Wild Shape",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\nAt 10th level, you can expend two uses of Wild Shape at the same time to transform into an air elemental, an earth elemental, a fire elemental, or a water elemental."},
  ["spell.elementalism.xphb2024"]={title="Elementalism",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 267\n\nYou exert control over the elements, creating one of the following effects within range.\n\nBeckon Air\n\nYou create a breeze strong enough to ripple cloth, stir dust, rustle leaves, and close open doors and shutters, all in a 5-foot XPHB. Doors and shutters being held open by someone or something aren't affected.\n\nBeckon Earth\n\nYou create a thin shroud of dust or sand that covers surfaces in a 5-foot-square area, or you cause a single word to appear in your handwriting in a patch of dirt or sand.\n\nBeckon Fire\n\nYou create a thin cloud of harmless embers and colored, scented smoke in a 5-foot XPHB. You choose the color and scent, and the embers can light candles, torches, or lamps in that area. The smoke's scent lingers for 1 minute.\n\nBeckon Water\n\nYou create a spray of cool mist that lightly dampens creatures and objects in a 5-foot XPHB. Alternatively, you create 1 cup of clean water either in an open container or on a surface, and the water evaporates in 1 minute.\n\nSculpt Element\n\nYou cause dirt, sand, fire, smoke, mist, or water that can fit in a 1-foot XPHB to assume a crude shape (such as that of a creature) for 1 hour."},
  ["creature.elephant.mm2014"]={title="Elephant",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 322\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 76 (8d12 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 17 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTrampling Charge\n\nIf the elephant moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 12 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the elephant can make one stomp attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (3d8 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. h22 (3d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.elephant.phb2014"]={title="Elephant",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.elephant.xmm2024"]={title="Elephant",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 353\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 76 (8d12 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 17 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe elephant makes two Gore attacks.\n\nGore\n\nm 8, reach 5 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Piercing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature and the elephant moved 20+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTrample\n\ndex 16, one creature within 5 feet that has the XPHB condition. actSaveFail 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["item.elephant.xphb2024"]={title="Elephant",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["species.elf.lfl2014"]={title="Elf",subtitle="Especie - LFL - 2014",body=""},
  ["species.elf.phb2014"]={title="Elf",subtitle="Especie - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nAge\n\nAlthough elves reach physical maturity at about the same age as humans, the elven understanding of adulthood goes beyond physical growth to encompass worldly experience. An elf typically claims adulthood and an adult name around the age of 100 and can live to be 750 years old.\n\nSize\n\nElves range from under 5 to over 6 feet tall and have slender builds. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nAccustomed to twilit forests and the night sky, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nKeen Senses\n\nYou have proficiency in the Perception skill.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.\n\nTrance\n\nElves don't need to sleep. Instead, they meditate deeply, remaining semiconscious, for 4 hours a day. (The Common word for such meditation is \"trance.\") While meditating, you can dream after a fashion; such dreams are actually mental exercises that have become reflexive through years of practice. After resting in this way, you gain the same benefit that a human does from 8 hours of sleep.\n\nIf you meditate during a long rest, you finish the rest after only 4 hours. You otherwise obey all the rules for a long rest; only the duration is changed.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Elvish. Elvish is fluid, with subtle intonations and intricate grammar. Elven literature is rich and varied, and their songs and poems are famous among other races. Many bards learn their language so they can add Elvish ballads to their repertoires."},
  ["species.elf.xphb2024"]={title="Elf",subtitle="Especie - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 189\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\nElven Lineage\n\nYou are part of a lineage that grants you supernatural abilities. Choose a lineage from the Elven Lineages table. You gain the level 1 benefit of that lineage.\n\nWhen you reach character levels 3 and 5, you learn a higher-level spell, as shown on the table. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level.\n\nIntelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for the spells you cast with this trait (choose the ability when you select the lineage).\n\nLineage | Level 1 | Level 3 | Level 5\n\nDrow | The range of your XPHB increases to 120 feet. You also know the XPHB cantrip. | XPHB | XPHB\n\nHigh Elf | You know the XPHB cantrip. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can replace that cantrip with a different spells. | XPHB | XPHB\n\nWood Elf | Your XPHB increases to 35 feet. You also know the XPHB cantrip. | XPHB | XPHB\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws you make to avoid or end the XPHB condition.\n\nKeen Senses\n\nYou have proficiency in the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB skill.\n\nTrance\n\nYou don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep. You can finish a XPHB in 4 hours if you spend those hours in a trancelike meditation, during which you retain consciousness."},
  ["species.elf-kaladesh.psk2014"]={title="Elf (Kaladesh)",subtitle="Especie - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nAge\n\nAlthough elves reach physical maturity at about the same age as humans, the elven understanding of adulthood goes beyond physical growth to encompass worldly experience. An elf typically claims adulthood and an adult name around the age of 100 and can live to be 750 years old.\n\nAlignment\n\nElves love freedom, variety, and self-expression, so they lean strongly toward the gentler aspects of chaos. They value and protect others' freedom as well as their own, and they are more often good than not.\n\nSize\n\nElves range from under 5 to over 6 feet tall and have slender builds. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nAccustomed to twilit forests and the night sky, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nKeen Senses\n\nYou have proficiency in the Perception skill.\n\nElf Weapon Training\n\nYou have proficiency with the phb, phb, phb, and phb.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.\n\nTrance\n\nElves don't need to sleep. Instead, they meditate deeply, remaining semiconscious, for 4 hours a day. (The Common word for such meditation is \"trance.\") While meditating, you can dream after a fashion; such dreams are actually mental exercises that have become reflexive through years of practice. After resting in this way, you gain the same benefit that a human does from 8 hours of sleep.\n\nIf you meditate during a long rest, you finish the rest after only 4 hours. You otherwise obey all the rules for a long rest; only the duration is changed.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Elvish. Elvish is fluid, with subtle intonations and intricate grammar. Elven literature is rich and varied, and their songs and poems are famous among other races. Many bards learn their language so they can add Elvish ballads to their repertoires.\n\nElf Culture\n\nThe elves of Kaladesh don't organize themselves into nations or tribes. Still, they recognize three distinct cultural groups among their kind—though in truth these groupings are more like attitudes or alignments with regard to the rest of society and the use of technology. Choose one of these cultures."},
  ["species.elf-zendikar.psz2014"]={title="Elf (Zendikar)",subtitle="Especie - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\nAge\n\nAlthough elves reach physical maturity at about the same age as humans, the elven understanding of adulthood goes beyond physical growth to encompass worldly experience. An elf typically claims adulthood and an adult name around the age of 100 and can live to be 750 years old.\n\nAlignment\n\nElves love freedom, variety, and self-expression, so they lean strongly toward the gentler aspects of chaos. They value and protect others' freedom as well as their own, and they are more often good than not.\n\nSize\n\nElves range from under 5 to over 6 feet tall and have slender builds. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nAccustomed to twilit forests and the night sky, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nKeen Senses\n\nYou have proficiency in the Perception skill.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Elvish. Elvish is fluid, with subtle intonations and intricate grammar. Elven literature is rich and varied, and their songs and poems are famous among other races. Many bards learn their language so they can add Elvish ballads to their repertoires."},
  ["creature.eliphas-adulare.kftgv2014"]={title="Eliphas Adulare",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 18\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)"},
  ["creature.elise.vrgr2014"]={title="Elise",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 143\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 9 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: cold, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nElise is immune to any spell or effect that would alter her form.\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever Elise is subjected to lightning damage, she takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nElise has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nElise's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nElise makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.elister.skt2014"]={title="Elister",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["magicitem.elixir-of-health.dmg2014"]={title="Elixir of Health",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhen you drink this potion, it cures any disease afflicting you, and it removes the blinded, deafened, paralyzed, and poisoned conditions. The clear red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it."},
  ["magicitem.elixir-of-health.xdmg2024"]={title="Elixir of Health",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 257\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhen you drink this potion, you are cured of all magical contagions. In addition, the following conditions end on you: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB.\n\nThe clear, red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it."},
  ["creature.elizar-dryflagon.pota2014"]={title="Elizar Dryflagon",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 71 (11d8 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 18 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSummon Mephits (Recharges after a Long Rest)\n\nBy puffing on his pipe, Elizar can use an action to cast conjure minor elementals. If he does so, he summons four smoke mephits.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger +1\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.elk.mm2014"]={title="Elk",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 322\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 13 (2d10 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the elk moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a ram attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. h8 (2d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["feature.elk.scag2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.3"]={title="Elk",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nWhile you're raging and aren't wearing heavy armor, your walking speed increases by 15 feet. The spirit of the elk makes you extraordinarily swift."},
  ["feature.elk.scag2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.6"]={title="Elk",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nWhether mounted or on foot, your travel pace is doubled, as is the travel pace of up to ten companions while they're within 60 feet of you and you're not incapacitated. The elk spirit helps you roam far and fast."},
  ["feature.elk.scag2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.14"]={title="Elk",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nWhile raging, you can use a bonus action during your move to pass through the space of a Large or smaller creature. That creature must succeed on a Strength saving throw (8 + your Strength bonus + your proficiency bonus) or be knocked prone and take bludgeoning damage equal to 1d12 + your Strength modifier."},
  ["creature.elk.xmm2024"]={title="Elk",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 353\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 11 (2d10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 11 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature and the elk moved 20+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 3 (1d6) Bludgeoning damage and has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.elkhorn.wbtw2014"]={title="Elkhorn",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 52 (7d8 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 9 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nElkhorn wields a +1 longsword.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nElkhorn makes two Dagger or +1 Longsword attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage. If the target is a creature that is Large or bigger, it takes an extra 5 (1d10) piercing damage.\n\n+1 Longsword\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) slashing damage, or 5 (1d10) slashing damage when used with two hands. If the target is a creature that is Large or bigger, it takes an extra 5 (1d10) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nFeint {@recharge 5}\n\nElkhorn targets one creature that he can see within 5 feet of him. Elkhorn has advantage on the next attack roll he makes against that target before the end of his turn. If that attack hits, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage of the weapon's type.\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nElkhorn regains 12 hit points."},
  ["creature.elliach.bgdia2014"]={title="Elliach",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.elminster-s-effulgent-spheres.frhof2014"]={title="Elminster's Effulgent Spheres",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nSix chromatic spheres orbit you for the duration.\n\nWhile the spheres are present, you can expend spheres to create the following effects:\n\n• Absorb Energy When you take Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage, you can take a XPHB to expend one sphere and give yourself XPHB to the triggering damage type until the start of your next turn.\n\n• Energy Blast As a XPHB, you send one sphere hurtling toward a target within 120 feet of yourself. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, the target takes 3d6 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (your choice). Regardless of whether you hit, the sphere is expended.\n\nThe spell ends early if you have no more spheres remaining."},
  ["spell.elminster-s-elusion.frhof2014"]={title="Elminster's Elusion",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nArcane wards protect you against magic for the duration. You have XPHB on saving throws against spells and magical effects. Additionally, if you succeed on a saving throw against a spell or magical effect and would normally take half as much damage, you instead take no damage."},
  ["magicitem.elocutionist-s-lexicon.au2014"]={title="Elocutionist's Lexicon",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhile holding this magic dictionary, you can take a XPHB action and try to recall a specific word. The book automatically opens to the page containing the exact word you're searching for."},
  ["creature.elok-jaharwon.toa2014"]={title="Elok Jaharwon",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 67\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.elusive.phb2014.rogue.base.18"]={title="Elusive",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nBeginning at 18th level, you are so evasive that attackers rarely gain the upper hand against you. No attack roll has advantage against you while you aren't incapacitated."},
  ["feature.elusive.xphb2024.rogue.base.18"]={title="Elusive",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 131\n\nYou're so evasive that attackers rarely gain the upper hand against you. No attack roll can have XPHB against you unless you have the XPHB condition."},
  ["charoption.elusive-paramour.idrotf2014"]={title="Elusive Paramour",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nA wealthy pasha in Calimshan has placed a bounty on my head for seducing his favorite concubine. Bounty hunters are scouring the Sword Coast in search of me, but I hope they'll never think to look in Icewind Dale."},
  ["feat.elven-accuracy.xge2024"]={title="Elven Accuracy",subtitle="Feat - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 74\n\nThe accuracy of elves is legendary, especially that of elf archers and spellcasters. You have uncanny aim with attacks that rely on precision rather than brute force. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• Whenever you have advantage on an attack roll using Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma, you can reroll one of the dice once."},
  ["magicitem.elven-chain.dmg2014"]={title="Elven Chain",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to AC while you wear this armor. You are considered proficient with this armor even if you lack proficiency with medium armor."},
  ["magicitem.elven-thrower.bgg2014"]={title="Elven Thrower",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. It has the thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When you hit with a ranged attack using this weapon, it deals an extra 1d8 damage or, if the target is a Giant, 2d8 damage. Immediately after the attack, the weapon flies back to your hand."},
  ["item.elven-trinket.mtf2014"]={title="Elven Trinket",subtitle="Item - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nRaridade: none\n\nd8 | Trinket\n\n1 | A small notebook that causes anything written in it to disappear after 1 hour\n\n2 | A crystal lens made of ivory and gold that causes anything observed through it to appear to be surrounded by motes of multicolored light\n\n3 | A small golden pyramid inscribed with elven symbols and about the size of a walnut\n\n4 | A cloak pin made from enamel in the shape of a butterfly; when you take the pin off, it turns into a real butterfly, and returns when you are ready to put your cloak back on again\n\n5 | A golden compass that points toward the nearest portal to the Feywild within 10 miles\n\n6 | A small silver spinning top that, when spun, endlessly spins until interrupted\n\n7 | A small songbird made of enamel, gold wire, and precious stone; uttering the songbird's name in Elvish causes the trinket to emit that bird's birdsong\n\n8 | A small enamel flower that, when put in one's hair, animates, tying back the wearer's hair with a living vine with flowers; plucking a single flower from this vine returns it to its inanimate form"},
  ["language.elvish.dsotdq2014"]={title="Elvish",subtitle="Idioma - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.elvish.erlw2014"]={title="Elvish",subtitle="Idioma - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 6"},
  ["language.elvish.ggr2014"]={title="Elvish",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.elvish.phb2014"]={title="Elvish",subtitle="Idioma - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 123\n\nElvish is fluid, with subtle intonations and intricate grammar. Elven literature is rich and varied, and their songs and poems are famous among other races. Many bards learn their language so they can add Elvish ballads to their repertoires."},
  ["language.elvish.xphb2024"]={title="Elvish",subtitle="Idioma - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 37"},
  ["creature.elzerina-cassalanter.wdh2014"]={title="Elzerina Cassalanter",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S"},
  ["creature.ember.mcv2dc2014"]={title="Ember",subtitle="Criatura - MCV2DC - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 270 (20d12 + 140)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCalescent Aura\n\nAt the start of Ember's turn, Ember can force any number of creatures of his choice within 10 feet of himself to make a 22 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 7 (2d6) fire damage and is frightened of Ember until the start of its next turn.\n\nLegendary Resistance (5/Day)\n\nIf Ember fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nIn battle, Ember dons magical plate armor custom-forged for his use. While wearing the armor, Ember adds his Charisma modifier to his weapon damage rolls (included in the attack descriptions), and his AC can't be lower than 20.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nEmber makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h26 (2d10 + 15) piercing damage plus 13 (2d6 + 6) fire damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h22 (2d6 + 15) slashing damage.\n\nFirestorm Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nEmber exhales roiling flames and ash in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 56 (16d6) fire damage and is pushed up to 30 feet away from Ember and knocked prone. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage with no other effects. If a creature is reduced to 0 hit points by this effect, the creature immediately dies, and its body is reduced to ash.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAlter Shape\n\nEmber magically transforms into a vulture or a mage and retains his alignment, damage immunities, hit points, and Hit Dice, as well as his Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. This transformation ends if Ember is reduced to 0 hit points or if he uses another bonus action to end it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPursuit\n\nEmber moves up to 40 feet in a straight line toward one creature he can see. This movement ignores opportunity attacks.\n\nSearing Bite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nEmber makes one Bite attack. If the attack hits, it deals an additional 7 (2d6) fire damage."},
  ["feat.ember-of-the-fire-giant.bgg2014"]={title="Ember of the Fire Giant",subtitle="Feat - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nYou've manifested the fiery combat emblematic of fire giants, granting you the following benefits:\n\n• Born of Flame You have resistance to fire damage.\n\n• Searing Ignition When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace a single attack with a magical burst of flame. Each creature of your choice in a 15-foot-radius sphere centered on you must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + the modifier of the ability increased by this feat). On a failed save, a creature takes fire damage equal to 1d8 + your proficiency bonus, and it has the blinded condition until the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. You can use your Searing Ignition a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus (but no more than once per turn), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["creature.emberhorn-minotaur.pota2014"]={title="Emberhorn Minotaur",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nImunidades: fire"},
  ["creature.emberosa.wdmm2014"]={title="Emberosa",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 221 (13d12 + 78)"},
  ["item.emblem.phb2014"]={title="Emblem",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.emblem.xphb2024"]={title="Emblem",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 226\n\nRaridade: none\n\nFor an Emblem to be an effective Holy Symbol, it must be borne on fabric (such as a tabard or banner) or a XPHB."},
  ["feature.embodiment-of-the-law.tce2014.cleric.order.6"]={title="Embodiment of the Law",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nAt 6th level, you become remarkably adept at channeling magical energy to compel others.\n\nIf you cast a spell of the enchantment school using a spell slot of 1st level or higher, you can change the spell's casting time to 1 bonus action for this casting, provided the spell's casting time is normally 1 action.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.emboldening-bond.tce2014.cleric.peace.1"]={title="Emboldening Bond",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.embric.wdh2014"]={title="Embric",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Primordial\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting"},
  ["item.embroidered-glove-set-with-jewel-chips.dmg2014"]={title="Embroidered glove set with jewel chips",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.embroidered-glove-set-with-jewel-chips.xdmg2024"]={title="Embroidered glove set with jewel chips",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.embroidered-silk-and-velvet-mantle-set-with-numerous-moonstones.dmg2014"]={title="Embroidered silk and velvet mantle set with numerous moonstones",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.embroidered-silk-and-velvet-mantle-set-with-numerous-moonstones.xdmg2024"]={title="Embroidered silk and velvet mantle set with numerous moonstones",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.embroidered-silk-handkerchief.dmg2014"]={title="Embroidered silk handkerchief",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.embroidered-silk-handkerchief.xdmg2024"]={title="Embroidered silk handkerchief",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.emerald.dmg2014"]={title="Emerald",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent deep bright green gemstone."},
  ["item.emerald.xdmg2024"]={title="Emerald",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA deep bright green gemstone."},
  ["creature.emerald-claw-commander.efa2014"]={title="Emerald Claw Commander",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 15 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Authority\n\nWhile in a 30-foot XPHB originating from the commander, the commander and its allies have XPHB on attack rolls and saving throws, provided the commander doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe commander makes two attacks, using Flail or Javelin in any combination.\n\nFlail\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage—plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage if the commander is Bloodied—and the target has XPHB on its next attack roll before the start of the commander's next turn.\n\nJavelin\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage—plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage if the commander is XPHB."},
  ["creature.emerald-claw-knight.efa2014"]={title="Emerald Claw Knight",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe knight makes two attacks, using Flail or Javelin in any combination.\n\nFlail\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage—plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage if the knight is Bloodied—and the target has XPHB on its next attack roll before the start of the knight's next turn.\n\nJavelin\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage—plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage if the knight is XPHB."},
  ["creature.emerald-dragon-wyrmling.ftd2014"]={title="Emerald Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20, fly: 60\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 14 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire, psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) psychic damage.\n\nDisorienting Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of psychic dissonance in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 17 (5d6) psychic damage, and until the end of its next turn, when the creature makes an attack roll or an ability check, it must roll a d4 and reduce the total by the number rolled. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects."},
  ["background.emerald-enclave-caretaker.frhof2014"]={title="Emerald Enclave Caretaker",subtitle="Background - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["feat.emerald-enclave-fledgling.frhof2014"]={title="Emerald Enclave Fledgling",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nSpeak with Animals\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it with any spell slots you have. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat). When you cast this spell as a XPHB, its duration is 8 hours.\n\nTag Team\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action, you can switch places with a willing ally within 5 feet of yourself as part of that same action. This movement doesn't provoke XPHB. You can't use this benefit if the ally has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.emerald-enclave-scout.oota2014"]={title="Emerald Enclave Scout",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nThe scout has advantage on saving throws against poison.\n\nKeen Hearing and Sight\n\nThe scout has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two melee attacks.\n\nWar Pick\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h5 (1d10) piercing damage."},
  ["item.emerald-enclave-trinket.frhof2014"]={title="Emerald Enclave Trinket",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: none\n\n1d6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A pair of earrings made from oak leaves that never wilt\n\n2 | A miniature model cottage made of twigs\n\n3 | A green-glowing firefly in a bottle\n\n4 | A gourd that sounds like rustling leaves when held to one's ear\n\n5 | A preserved rabbit's foot on a leather strap\n\n6 | An antler shaped like an Elvish rune"},
  ["creature.emerald-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Emerald Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 30 | WIS 24 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGem Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 400 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use its Mass Telekinesis action during the next hour. Award a party an additional 90,000 XP (180,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Gem Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 19) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales crushing force in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 71 (11d12) force damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone. On a success or failure, the creature's speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn.\n\nMass Telekinesis (Gem Awakening Only; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe greatwyrm targets any number of creatures and objects it can see within 120 feet of it. No one target can weigh more than 4,000 pounds, and objects can't be targeted if they're being worn or carried. Each targeted creature must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be restrained in the greatwyrm's telekinetic grip. At the end of a creature's turn, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nAt the end of the greatwyrm's turn, it can move each creature or object it has in its telekinetic grip up to 60 feet in any direction, but not beyond 120 feet of itself. In addition, it can choose any number of creatures restrained in this way and deal 45 (7d12) force damage to each of them.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the greatwyrm is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe greatwyrm magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nPsychic Beam (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm emits a beam of psychic energy in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Intelligence saving throw, taking 27 (5d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["magicitem.emerald-pen.ftd2014"]={title="Emerald Pen",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis pen is tipped with an emerald nib and requires no ink to write. While holding this pen, you can cast illusory script at will, requiring no material components."},
  ["creature.emil-toranescu.cos2014"]={title="Emil Toranescu",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 72 (9d8 + 18)"},
  ["feature.emissary-of-peace.xge2024.paladin.redemption.3"]={title="Emissary of Peace",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 38\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to augment your presence with divine power. As a bonus action, you grant yourself a +5 bonus to Charisma (Persuasion) checks for the next 10 minutes."},
  ["feature.emissary-of-redemption.xge2024.paladin.redemption.20"]={title="Emissary of Redemption",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 38\n\nAt 20th level, you become an avatar of peace, which gives you two benefits:\n\n• You have resistance to all damage dealt by other creatures (their attacks, spells, and other effects).\n\n• Whenever a creature hits you with an attack, it takes radiant damage equal to half the damage you take from the attack.\n\nIf you attack a creature, cast a spell on it, or deal damage to it by any means but this feature, neither benefit works against that creature until you finish a long rest."},
  ["creature.emmek-frewn.wdh2014"]={title="Emmek Frewn",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.emo.nrh-at2014"]={title="Emo",subtitle="Criatura - NRH-AT - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.empowered-channeling.rhw2014.bard.spirits.6"]={title="Empowered Channeling",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.empowered-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.10"]={title="Empowered Evocation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nBeginning at 10th level, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of any wizard evocation spell you cast."},
  ["feature.empowered-evocation.xphb2024.wizard.evoker.10"]={title="Empowered Evocation",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.empowered-healing.xge2024.sorcerer.divine-soul.6"]={title="Empowered Healing",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 50\n\nStarting at 6th level, the divine energy coursing through you can empower healing spells. Whenever you or an ally within 5 feet of you rolls dice to determine the number of hit points a spell restores, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll any number of those dice once, provided you aren't incapacitated. You can use this feature only once per turn."},
  ["optionalfeature.empowered-spell.phb2014"]={title="Empowered Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\nWhen you roll damage for a spell, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.\n\nYou can use Empowered Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell."},
  ["optionalfeature.empowered-spell.xphb2024"]={title="Empowered Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 142\n\nWhen you roll damage for a spell, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point to reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one), and you must use the new rolls.\n\nYou can use Empowered Spell even if you've already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell."},
  ["feature.empowered-spells.tce2014.spellcaster-sidekick.base.14"]={title="Empowered Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n14th-level Spellcaster feature\n\nChoose one school of magic. Whenever the sidekick casts a spell of that school by expending a spell slot, the sidekick can add its spellcasting ability modifier to the spell's damage roll or healing roll, if any."},
  ["feature.empowered-strikes.xphb2024.monk.base.6"]={title="Empowered Strikes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.empowered-transmutation.au2014.wizard.transmuter.6"]={title="Empowered Transmutation",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.empty-body.phb2014.monk.base.18"]={title="Empty Body",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nBeginning at 18th level, you can use your action to spend 4 ki points to become invisible for 1 minute. During that time, you also have resistance to all damage but force damage.\n\nAdditionally, you can spend 8 ki points to cast the astral projection spell, without needing material components. When you do so, you can't take any other creatures with you."},
  ["creature.empty-echo.pl2014"]={title="Empty Echo",subtitle="Criatura - PL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S/M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 6 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe echo can't shape-shift.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nStatic Scream {@recharge}\n\ncon 11, each creature of the echo's choice within 30 feet. actSaveFail 5 (2d4) Thunder damage, and the creature has the XPHB condition until the start of the echo's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAutomated Self-Preservation\n\nThe echo takes the Dash or Disengage action."},
  ["creature.empyrean.mm2014"]={title="Empyrean",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / H\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 313 (19d12 + 190)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, fly: 50, swim: 50\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 21 | CON 30 | INT 21 | WIS 22 | CHA 27\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nImunidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the empyrean fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe empyrean has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe empyrean's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMaul\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h31 (6d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of the empyrean's next turn.\n\nBolt\n\nrs 15 to hit, range 600 ft., one target. h24 (7d6) damage of one of the following types (empyrean's choice): acid, cold, fire, force, lightning, radiant, or thunder.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe empyrean makes one attack.\n\nBolster\n\nThe empyrean bolsters all nonhostile creatures within 120 feet of it until the end of its next turn. Bolstered creatures can't be charmed or frightened, and they gain advantage on ability checks and saving throws until the end of the empyrean's next turn.\n\nTrembling Strike (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe empyrean strikes the ground with its maul, triggering an earth tremor. All other creatures on the ground within 60 feet of the empyrean must succeed on a 25 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.empyrean.xmm2024"]={title="Empyrean",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 113\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: {'choose': ['celestial', 'fiend']} / H\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 346 (21d12 + 210)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, fly: 50, swim: 50\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 21 | CON 30 | INT 21 | WIS 22 | CHA 27\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: necrotic, radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the empyrean fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe empyrean has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe empyrean makes two attacks, using Sacred Weapon or Divine Ray in any combination.\n\nSacred Weapon\n\nm 17, reach 10 ft. h31 (6d6 + 10) Force damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the empyrean's next turn. The target can choose not to be XPHB, in which case it takes an extra 21 Force damage that bypasses XPHB or XPHB.\n\nDivine Ray\n\nr 15, range 600 ft. h35 (6d8 + 8) Necrotic or Radiant damage (empyrean's choice).\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBolster\n\nThe empyrean gains 10 XPHB, and the empyrean and each ally within 30 feet of it gain XPHB on XPHB until the end of the empyrean's next turn. The empyrean can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nShockwave of Glory\n\ncon 23, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB originating from the empyrean. actSaveFail 27 (6d8) Force damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail The empyrean can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nSmite\n\nThe empyrean makes one Divine Ray attack."},
  ["creature.empyrean-iota.xmm2024"]={title="Empyrean Iota",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: {'choose': ['celestial', 'fiend']} / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 30\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades a condicoes: prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe empyrean can move through other creatures and objects as if they were XPHB. It takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe empyrean has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nHealing Word (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nOtherworldly Strike\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Necrotic or Radiant damage (empyrean's choice)."},
  ["creature.emrakul.psz2014"]={title="Emrakul",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.encephalon-cluster.pabtso2014"]={title="Encephalon Cluster",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 110 (17d10 + 17)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 13 | INT 5 | WIS 17 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (can't see beyond this radius)\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the cluster fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe cluster has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cluster makes two Slam attacks. It can replace one of these attacks with Spawn Progeny if available.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage, and if the target is a creature, the target must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition. If this attack reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target immediately dies and is consumed by the cluster.\n\nSpawn Progeny (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe cluster bulges and spews 1d4 mature eggs. Each egg lands in an unoccupied space of the cluster's choice within 30 feet of itself and immediately transforms into an PaBTSO. The gemmules obey the cluster's commands and take their turns immediately after it.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nAggressive Hunger\n\nImmediately after being hit by an attack, the cluster moves up to its speed toward the attacker. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks. If the cluster ends this movement within 5 feet of the attacker, it then makes one Slam attack against that attacker."},
  ["creature.encephalon-gemmule.pabtso2014"]={title="Encephalon Gemmule",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / T\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 54 (12d4 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (can't see beyond this radius)\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEncephalon Progeny\n\nThe gemmule matures into an encephalon cluster if not killed within 30 (4d12 + 4) days of its creation.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe gemmule has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPsychic Slam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (3d10) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeech\n\nThe gemmule targets one creature within 5 feet of itself and forces the target to make a 14 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the gemmule enters the target's space and attaches to the target. While the gemmule is attached, the target takes 7 (3d4) piercing damage at the start of each of its turns, and the gemmule can't use Leech again until it detaches. It can detach itself by spending 5 feet of its movement. As an action, the target or a creature within 5 feet of the target can detach the gemmule by succeeding on a 15 Strength check."},
  ["object.enchanted-ballista.hbtd2014"]={title="Enchanted Ballista",subtitle="Objeto - HBTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 4\n\nLoading the Enchanted Ballista requires the XPHB action. Then a creature can take the Ballista Bolt action."},
  ["item.enchanted-three-dragon-ante-set.llk2014"]={title="Enchanted Three-Dragon Ante Set",subtitle="Item - LLK - 2014",body="Pagina: 15"},
  ["subclass.enchanter.au2014.wizard.enchanter.0"]={title="Enchanter",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Enchanter\n\nPagina: 16\n\nEntrance and Beguile Others\n\nAn Enchanter's magic clouds or captivates minds. Some Enchanters use their abilities to encourage peace and soften cruelty, while others use their mind-altering magic for selfish ends.\n\nNivel 3 - Enchanting Conversationalist\n\nPagina: 16\n\nYou gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB.\n\nIn addition, when you make an ability check with the chosen skill, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nNivel 3 - Enchantment Savant\n\nPagina: 16\n\nChoose two spells, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.\n\nIn addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one spells to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nNivel 3 - Hypnotic Presence\n\nPagina: 17\n\nYour charming words and enchanting gaze can enthrall another creature. As a XPHB action, choose one creature that you can see within 10 feet of yourself. If the target can see or hear you, it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or have the XPHB condition for 1 minute or until the target is more than 10 feet away from you, the target can neither see nor hear you, or the target takes damage. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition and a XPHB of 0.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Hypnotic Presence\n\nNivel 6 - Split Enchantment\n\nPagina: 17\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast an spells, such as XPHB, that can be cast with a higher-level spell slot to target an additional creature, you can increase the spell's effective level by 1.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Split Enchantment\n\nNivel 10 - Instinctive Charm\n\nPagina: 17\n\nWhen a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see hits you with an attack roll, you can take a XPHB to force the attacker to make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the attack misses instead, and if there is another creature within range of the attack other than the attacker, the attacker targets that creature with the triggering attack, using the same attack roll. If multiple creatures are within the attack's range, you choose which one to target.\n\nOnce you take this XPHB, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB. You can also restore your use of it by casting an spells with a spell slot.\n\nNivel 10 - Instinctive Charm\n\nNivel 14 - Alter Memories\n\nPagina: 17\n\nYou can make a creature unaware of your magical influence. When you cast an spells that imposes the XPHB condition using a spell slot, you can choose one creature targeted by the spell. That creature remains unaware of being XPHB by you.\n\nIn addition, once before the spell ends, you can take a XPHB action to force the chosen creature to make an Intelligence saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you can make the creature lose a number of hours of its memories equal to 1 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 hour lost). You can make the creature forget less time, and the amount of time can't exceed the duration of your spells.\n\nNivel 14 - Alter Memories"},
  ["feature.enchanter.au2014.wizard.enchanter.3"]={title="Enchanter",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nEntrance and Beguile Others\n\nAn Enchanter's magic clouds or captivates minds. Some Enchanters use their abilities to encourage peace and soften cruelty, while others use their mind-altering magic for selfish ends."},
  ["creature.enchanter.vgm2014"]={title="Enchanter",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d8 - 1) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nInstinctive Charm (Recharges after the Enchanter Casts an Enchantment Spell of 1st level or Higher)\n\nThe enchanter tries to magically divert an attack made against it, provided that the attacker is within 30 feet of it and visible to it. The enchanter must decide to do so before the attack hits or misses.\n\nThe attacker must make a 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the attacker targets the creature closest to it, other than the enchanter or itself. If multiple creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target."},
  ["creature.enchanter-archmage.au2014"]={title="Enchanter Archmage",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 137\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 214 (39d8 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus five other languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archmage has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nDominate Person (1/Day)\n\nDuplicitous Magic (2/Day)\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archmage makes four Arcane Burst Attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 10, reach 5 ft. or range 150 ft. h21 (3d10 + 5) Force damage."},
  ["creature.enchanter-wizard.mpmm2014"]={title="Enchanter Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 261\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 49 (11d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe enchanter makes three Arcane Burst attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h19 (3d10 + 3) psychic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nInstinctive Charm {@recharge 4}\n\nWhen a visible creature within 30 feet of the enchanter makes an attack roll against it, the enchanter forces the attacker to make a 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the attacker redirects the attack roll to the creature closest to it, other than the enchanter or itself. If multiple eligible creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target."},
  ["feature.enchanting-conversationalist.au2014.wizard.enchanter.3"]={title="Enchanting Conversationalist",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nYou gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB.\n\nIn addition, when you make an ability check with the chosen skill, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1)."},
  ["creature.enchanting-infiltrator.bmt2014"]={title="Enchanting Infiltrator",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S/M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 156 (24d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 20 | CON 15 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, thieves' cant, plus any one language\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the infiltrator fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nVeiled Presence\n\nThe infiltrator's AC includes its Wisdom modifier, and the infiltrator can't be targeted by divination magic or features that would read its mind or determine its creature type.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe infiltrator makes two Poison Blade attacks and can use Beguiling Whisper.\n\nPoison Blade\n\nmw,rw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h7 (1d4 + 5) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) poison damage.\n\nBeguiling Whisper\n\nThe infiltrator magically whispers to a creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or have the stunned condition due to fear or delight (the infiltrator's choice) until the end of the target's next turn, after which the target is immune to this Beguiling Whisper for 24 hours.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nWhen an attacker the infiltrator can see hits the infiltrator with an attack, the infiltrator halves the attack's damage against it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCunning\n\nThe infiltrator escapes nonmagical restraints and ends the grappled condition on itself, then moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nStab (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe infiltrator makes one Poison Blade attack.\n\nMisdirecting Escape (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe infiltrator magically has the invisible condition and creates an illusory duplicate of itself in its space, then teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, to an unoccupied space within 15 feet of itself. The image flings illusory blades at two creatures of the infiltrator's choice within 20 feet of the image. Each target must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw, taking 13 (3d8) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The invisibility lasts until the end of the infiltrator's next turn."},
  ["feat.enchantment-adept.au2014"]={title="Enchantment Adept",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAdditional Spells\n\nYour prowess allows you to always have certain spells at the ready. When you have spell slots of a level specified in the Enchantment Adept Spells table, you thereafter always have the spells listed for that level and lower prepared.\n\nSubtle Enchantments\n\nWhen you cast a spell from the Enchantment school using a spell slot, you can cast it without any Verbal, Somatic, or Material components, except Material components that are consumed by the spell or that have a cost specified in the spell.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Spell\n\n1 | XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feature.enchantment-savant.au2014.wizard.enchanter.3"]={title="Enchantment Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nChoose two spells, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.\n\nIn addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one spells to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots."},
  ["feature.enchantment-savant.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.2"]={title="Enchantment Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy an enchantment spell into your spellbook is halved."},
  ["feat.enclave-magic.frhof2014"]={title="Enclave Magic",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nFriend to Animals\n\nYou have XPHB on ability checks when taking the XPHB action with Beasts.\n\nTwo Hearts, One Mind\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. When you cast it without a spell slot using this feature, it doesn't require XPHB. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. The spell's spellcasting ability is the ability increased by this feat."},
  ["spell.encode-thoughts.ggr2014"]={title="Encode Thoughts",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\nPutting a finger to your head, you pull a memory, an idea, or a message from your mind and transform it into a tangible string of glowing energy called a thought strand, which persists for the duration or until you cast this spell again. The thought strand appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you as a Tiny, weightless, semisolid object that can be held and carried like a ribbon. It is otherwise stationary.\n\nIf you cast this spell while concentration on a spell or an ability that allows you to read or manipulate the thoughts of others (such as detect thoughts or modify memory), you can transform the thoughts or memories you read, rather than your own, into a thought strand.\n\nCasting this spell while holding a thought strand allows you to instantly receive whatever memory, idea, or message the thought strand contains. (Casting detect thoughts on the strand has the same effect.)"},
  ["actionref.end-concentration.phb2014"]={title="End Concentration",subtitle="Acao - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\nIf a spell must be maintained with concentration, that fact appears in its Duration entry, and the spell specifies how long you can concentrate on it. You can end concentration at any time (no action required)."},
  ["actionref.end-concentration.xphb2024"]={title="End Concentration",subtitle="Acao - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 363\n\nSome spells and other effects require Concentration to remain active, as specified in their descriptions. You can end Concentration at any time (no action required)."},
  ["creature.endelyn-moongrave.wbtw2014"]={title="Endelyn Moongrave",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 114 (12d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 13 | CON 20 | INT 13 | WIS 10 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBoon of Immortality\n\nEndelyn is immune to any effect that would age her, and she can't die from old age.\n\nEclipsed Doom\n\nEndelyn can be killed only if she is reduced to 0 hit points during a solar eclipse or while she is within 60 feet of a symbolic representation of one. Otherwise, Endelyn disappears in a cloud of inky smoke when she drops to 0 hit points, along with anything she was wearing or carrying, and reappears 24 hours later in the same location or the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nUncanny Awareness\n\nEndelyn can't be surprised.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nEndelyn makes two Puppeteer's Lash attacks\n\nPuppeteer's Lash\n\nms,rs 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one creature. h17 (4d6 + 3) psychic damage, and if the target is Large or smaller, Endelyn telekinetically moves it up to 10 feet in any direction horizontally."},
  ["creature.ender-dragon.mcv3mc2014"]={title="Ender Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MCV3MC - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 19\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 350 (20d20 + 140)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 120\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDragon Egg\n\nWhen the Ender Dragon drops to 0 hit points, it radiates beams of purple light and then disappears, leaving behind an inert, jet-black dragon egg worth 5,000 gp.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and uses Beating Wings.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit; reach 15 ft., one target. h18 (3d6 + 8) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage.\n\nBeating Wings\n\nThe dragon beats its great wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 21 Dexterity saving throw or take 10 (1d4 + 8) bludgeoning damage, be pushed 10 feet away from the dragon, and have the prone condition.\n\nHarmful Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales putrid gas in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 21 Constitution saving throw, taking 52 (15d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The dragon then chooses a point it can see where the cone makes contact with the ground. That point becomes the center of a 10-foot-high, 10-foot-radius cylinder of lingering gas that disappears at the start of the dragon's next turn. Any creature that starts its turn in the cylinder takes 10 (3d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.enderman.mcv3mc2014"]={title="Enderman",subtitle="Criatura - MCV3MC - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 18 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Endspeech\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasive Teleportation\n\nWhenever it takes damage or is the target of a ranged attack, the Enderman can teleport, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, to an unoccupied space it can see within 20 feet of itself (no action required). If this effect is triggered by a ranged attack, the Enderman teleports just before the attack hits, causing the attack to miss it. This trait is suppressed while the Enderman has the incapacitated condition.\n\nImplosion\n\nWhen the Enderman drops to 0 hit points, it dies as its body implodes. Roll a d10. On a roll of 9 or less, the Enderman leaves no remains. On a roll of 10, the Enderman leaves behind a glowing, purple orb called an Ender pearl, worth 500 gp. A creature can throw the pearl up to 60 feet; if the pearl lands in an unoccupied space big enough to contain the creature, the creature teleports to that space, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, and the pearl disappears.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the Enderman has disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\nWater Susceptibility\n\nThe Enderman takes 1 cold damage for every 5 feet it moves in water, for every gallon of water splashed on it, or whenever it starts its turn in the rain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Enderman makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit; reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage."},
  ["magicitem.enduring-spellbook.xdmg2024"]={title="Enduring Spellbook",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 257\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis spellbook, along with anything written on its pages, can't be damaged by fire or water. In addition, the spellbook doesn't deteriorate with age."},
  ["magicitem.enduring-spellbook.xge2024"]={title="Enduring Spellbook",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 137\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis spellbook, along with anything written on its pages, can't be damaged by fire or immersion in water. In addition, the spellbook doesn't deteriorate with age."},
  ["spell.enemies-abound.xge2024"]={title="Enemies Abound",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nYou reach into the mind of one creature you can see and force it to make an Intelligence saving throw. A creature automatically succeeds if it is immune to being frightened. On a failed save, the target loses the ability to distinguish friend from foe, regarding all creatures it can see as enemies until the spell ends. Each time the target takes damage, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nWhenever the affected creature chooses another creature as a target, it must choose the target at random from among the creatures it can see within range of the attack, spell, or other ability it's using. If an enemy provokes an opportunity attack from the affected creature, the creature must make that attack if it is able to."},
  ["psionic.energy-beam.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Energy Beam",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nAs an action, you target one creature you can see within 90 feet of you. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage (your choice).\n\nThe talent's damage increases by 1d8 when you reach 5th level (2d8), 11th level (3d8), and 17th level (4d8)."},
  ["item.energy-cell.dmg2014"]={title="Energy Cell",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.energy-cell.xdmg2024"]={title="Energy Cell",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 72\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.enervation.au2014"]={title="Enervation",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nA tendril of inky darkness reaches out from you to drain life from a creature you can see within range.\n\nThe target makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 6d8 Necrotic damage. On each of your subsequent turns, you can take a XPHB to deal 2d8 Necrotic damage to the target automatically. The spell ends if the target is ever outside the spell's range or it has XPHB from you.\n\nOn a successful save, the target takes half the initial damage only, and the spell ends.\n\nWhenever this spell deals damage to a target, you regain XPHB equal to half the amount of Necrotic damage dealt."},
  ["spell.enervation.xge2024"]={title="Enervation",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nA tendril of inky darkness reaches out from you, touching a creature you can see within range to drain life from it. The target must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a successful save, the target takes 2d8 necrotic damage, and the spell ends. On a failed save, the target takes 4d8 necrotic damage, and until the spell ends, you can use your action on each of your turns to automatically deal 4d8 necrotic damage to the target. The spell ends if you use your action to do anything else, if the target is ever outside the spell's range, or if the target has Cover from you.\n\nWhenever the spell deals damage to a target, you regain hit points equal to half the amount of necrotic damage the target takes."},
  ["optionalfeature.enfeebling-arrow.xge2024"]={title="Enfeebling Arrow",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 29\n\nYou weave necromantic magic into your arrow. The creature hit by the arrow takes an extra 2d6 necrotic damage. The target must also succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or the damage dealt by its weapon attacks is halved until the start of your next turn.\n\nThe necrotic damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class."},
  ["optionalfeature.enfeebling-shot.au2014"]={title="Enfeebling Shot",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYour ammunition saps your target's strength. The creature you hit takes extra Necrotic damage equal to two rolls of your Arcane Shot Die. The target must also succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. Whenever a target XPHB in this way hits with an attack roll, it subtracts an amount equal to one roll of your Arcane Shot Die from the total damage of that attack."},
  ["creature.engineer.wdh2014"]={title="Engineer",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nIdiomas: Common, Gnomish"},
  ["spell.enhance-ability.phb2014"]={title="Enhance Ability",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\nYou touch a creature and bestow upon it a magical enhancement. Choose one of the following effects; the target gains that effect until the spell ends.\n\nBear's Endurance\n\nThe target has advantage on Constitution checks. It also gains 2d6 temporary hit points, which are lost when the spell ends.\n\nBull's Strength\n\nThe target has advantage on Strength checks, and his or her carrying capacity doubles.\n\nCat's Grace\n\nThe target has advantage on Dexterity checks. It also doesn't take damage from falling 20 feet or less if it isn't incapacitated.\n\nEagle's Splendor\n\nThe target has advantage on Charisma checks.\n\nFox's Cunning\n\nThe target has advantage on Intelligence checks.\n\nOwl's Wisdom\n\nThe target has advantage on Wisdom checks."},
  ["spell.enhance-ability.xphb2024"]={title="Enhance Ability",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\nYou touch a creature and choose Strength, Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. For the duration, the target has XPHB on ability checks using the chosen ability."},
  ["optionalfeature.enhanced-arcane-focus.tce2014"]={title="Enhanced Arcane Focus",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nWhile holding this item, a creature gains a +1 bonus to spell attack rolls. In addition, the creature ignores Cover when making a spell attack.\n\nThe bonus increases to +2 when you reach 10th level in this class."},
  ["feature.enhanced-bond.tce2014.druid.wildfire.6"]={title="Enhanced Bond",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n6th-level Circle of Wildfire feature\n\nThe bond with your wildfire spirit enhances your destructive and restorative spells. Whenever you cast a spell that deals fire damage or restores hit points while your wildfire spirit is summoned, roll a d8, and you gain a bonus equal to the number rolled to one damage or healing roll of the spell.\n\nIn addition, when you cast a spell with a range other than self, the spell can originate from you or your wildfire spirit."},
  ["optionalfeature.enhanced-defense.tce2014"]={title="Enhanced Defense",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nA creature gains a +1 bonus to Armor Class while wearing (armor) or wielding (shield) the infused item.\n\nThe bonus increases to +2 when you reach 10th level in this class."},
  ["creature.enhanced-medusa.imr2014"]={title="Enhanced Medusa",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPetrifying Gaze\n\nWhen a creature that can see the medusa's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of the medusa, the medusa can force it to make a 14 Constitution saving throw if the medusa isn't incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is instantly petrified. Otherwise, a creature that fails the save begins to turn to metal, wood, or porcelain (the medusa's choice) and is restrained. The restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on a failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until the creature is freed by the greater restoration spell or other magic.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it can't see the medusa until the start of its next turn, when it can avert its eyes again. If the creature looks at the medusa in the meantime, it must immediately make the save.\n\nIf the medusa sees itself reflected on a polished surface within 30 feet of it and in an area of bright light, the medusa is, due to its curse, affected by its own gaze.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting"},
  ["optionalfeature.enhanced-weapon.tce2014"]={title="Enhanced Weapon",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nThis magic weapon grants a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it.\n\nThe bonus increases to +2 when you reach 10th level in this class."},
  ["spell.enlarge-reduce.phb2014"]={title="Enlarge/Reduce",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\nYou cause a creature or an object you can see within range to grow larger or smaller for the duration. Choose either a creature or an object that is neither worn nor carried. If the target is unwilling, it can make a Constitution saving throw. On a success, the spell has no effect.\n\nIf the target is a creature, everything it is wearing and carrying changes size with it. Any item dropped by an affected creature returns to normal size at once.\n\nEnlarge\n\nThe target's size doubles in all dimensions, and its weight is multiplied by eight. This growth increases its size by one category—from Medium to Large, for example. If there isn't enough room for the target to double its size, the creature or object attains the maximum possible size in the space available. Until the spell ends, the target also has advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The target's weapons also grow to match its new size. While these weapons are enlarged, the target's attacks with them deal 1d4 extra damage.\n\nReduce\n\nThe target's size is halved in all dimensions, and its weight is reduced to one-eighth of normal. This reduction decreases its size by one category—from Medium to Small, for example. Until the spell ends, the target also has disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The target's weapons also shrink to match its new size. While these weapons are reduced, the target's attacks with them deal 1d4 less damage (this can't reduce the damage below 1)."},
  ["spell.enlarge-reduce.xphb2024"]={title="Enlarge/Reduce",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\nFor the duration, the spell enlarges or reduces a creature or an object you can see within range (see the chosen effect below). A targeted object must be neither worn nor carried. If the target is an unwilling creature, it can make a Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the spell has no effect.\n\nEverything that a targeted creature is wearing and carrying changes size with it. Any item it drops returns to normal size at once. A thrown weapon or piece of ammunition returns to normal size immediately after it hits or misses a target.\n\nEnlarge\n\nThe target's size increases by one category—from Medium to Large, for example. The target also has XPHB on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The target's attacks with its enlarged weapons or Unarmed Strikes deal an extra 1d4 damage on a hit.\n\nReduce\n\nThe target's size decreases by one category—from Medium to Small, for example. The target also has XPHB on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The target's attacks with its reduced weapons or Unarmed Strikes deal 1d4 less damage on a hit (this can't reduce the damage below 1)."},
  ["creature.enna-galakiir-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Enna Galakiir (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.enna-galakiir-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Enna Galakiir (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.enna-galakiir-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Enna Galakiir (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.enormous-tentacle.oow2014"]={title="Enormous Tentacle",subtitle="Criatura - OoW - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nReach\n\nThe tentacle can reach anywhere in the room.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 35 ft., one creature. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 16). Until this grapple ends, the creature is restrained, and the tentacle can't constrict another target."},
  ["spell.ensnaring-strike.phb2014"]={title="Ensnaring Strike",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\nThe next time you hit a creature with a weapon attack before this spell ends, a writhing mass of thorny vines appears at the point of impact, and the target must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be restrained by the magical vines until the spell ends. A Large or larger creature has advantage on this saving throw. If the target succeeds on the save, the vines shrivel away.\n\nWhile restrained by this spell, the target takes 1d6 piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. A creature restrained by the vines or one that can touch the creature can use its action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC. On a success, the target is freed."},
  ["spell.ensnaring-strike.xphb2024"]={title="Ensnaring Strike",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\nAs you hit the target, grasping vines appear on it, and it makes a Strength saving throw. A Large or larger creature has XPHB on this save. On a failed save, the target has the XPHB condition until the spell ends. On a successful save, the vines shrivel away, and the spell ends.\n\nWhile XPHB, the target takes 1d6 Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. The target or a creature within reach of it can take an action to make a Strength (XPHB) check against your spell save DC. On a success, the spell ends."},
  ["magicitem.ensorcelled-missive.au2014"]={title="Ensorcelled Missive",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis item functions as a sheet of Parchment. After writing on it, you can take a XPHB action to fold or roll the sheet and seal it while speaking or signing a word or short phrase. If a creature unseals the sheet without using the same word or phrase, the writing on the sheet appears as if it were written in an unknown and unintelligible script."},
  ["magicitem.enspelled-staff-cantrip.xdmg2024"]={title="Enspelled Staff (Cantrip)",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 258\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nBound into this staff is a cantrip. The cantrip is determined when the staff is created and can be of any school of magic. The staff has 6 charges and regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding the staff, you can expend 1 charge to cast its spell. If you expend the staff's last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff loses its properties and becomes a nonmagical XPHB.\n\nThe spell's saving throw DC is 13, and its attack bonus is 5."},
  ["magicitem.enspelled-staff-level-1.xdmg2024"]={title="Enspelled Staff (Level 1)",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 258\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nBound into this staff is a spells. The spell is determined when the staff is created and can be of any school of magic. The staff has 6 charges and regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding the staff, you can expend 1 charge to cast its spell. If you expend the staff's last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff loses its properties and becomes a nonmagical XPHB.\n\nThe spell's saving throw DC is 13, and its attack bonus is 5."},
