  ["creature.fhenimore.lr2014"]={title="Fhenimore",subtitle="Criatura - LR - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nCA: 13\n\nSTR 16\n\nIdiomas: Common, Aquan"},
  ["creature.fidelio.wdmm2014"]={title="Fidelio",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 80 (10d8)\n\nIdiomas: Common"},
  ["creature.fiend-cultist.xmm2024"]={title="Fiend Cultist",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 87\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 18 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 90 ft. (unimpeded by magical {@variantrule Darkness|XPHB})\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nHellish Rebuke\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cultist makes three Pact Axe attacks.\n\nPact Axe\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) Fire damage."},
  ["subclass.fiend-patron.xphb2024.warlock.fiend.0"]={title="Fiend Patron",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Dark One's Blessing\n\nPagina: 109\n\nStarting at 1st level, when you reduce a hostile creature to 0 hit points, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Charisma modifier + your warlock level (minimum of 1).\n\nNivel 1 - The Fiend\n\nPagina: 109\n\nYou have made a pact with a fiend from the lower planes of existence, a being whose aims are evil, even if you strive against those aims. Such beings desire the corruption or destruction of all things, ultimately including you. Fiends powerful enough to forge a pact include demon lords such as Demogorgon, Orcus, Fraz-Urb'luu, and Baphomet; archdevils such as Asmodeus, Dispater, Mephistopheles, and Belial; pit fiends and balors that are especially mighty; and ultroloths and other lords of the yugoloths.\n\nExpanded Spell List\n\nThe Fiend lets you choose from an expanded list of spells when you learn a warlock spell. The following spells are added to the warlock spell list for you.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1st | burning hands, command\n\n2nd | blindness/deafness, scorching ray\n\n3rd | fireball, stinking cloud\n\n4th | fire shield, wall of fire\n\n5th | flame strike, hallow\n\nNivel 3 - Dark One's Blessing\n\nPagina: 161\n\nWhen you reduce an enemy to 0 XPHB, you gain XPHB equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Warlock level (minimum of 1 XPHB). You also gain this benefit if someone else reduces an enemy within 10 feet of you to 0 XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Dark One's Blessing\n\nNivel 3 - Fiend Patron\n\nPagina: 161\n\nMake a Deal with the Lower Planes\n\nYour pact draws on the Lower Planes, the realms of perdition. You might forge a bargain with a demon lord such as Demogorgon or Orcus; an archdevil such as Asmodeus; or a pit fiend, balor, yugoloth, or night hag that is especially mighty. That patron's aims are evil—the corruption or destruction of all things, ultimately including you—and your path is defined by the extent to which you strive against those aims.\n\nNivel 3 - Fiend Spells\n\nPagina: 161\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Fiend Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - The Fiend\n\nNivel 6 - Dark One's Own Luck\n\nPagina: 109\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can call on your patron to alter fate in your favor. When you make an ability check or a saving throw, you can use this feature to add a d10 to your roll. You can do so after seeing the initial roll but before any of the roll's effects occur.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNivel 6 - Dark One's Own Luck\n\nPagina: 162\n\nYou can call on your fiendish patron to alter fate in your favor. When you make an ability check or a saving throw, you can use this feature to add 1d10 to your roll. You can do so after seeing the roll but before any of the roll's effects occur.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), but you can use it no more than once per roll. You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Dark One's Own Luck\n\nNivel 10 - Fiendish Resilience\n\nPagina: 109\n\nStarting at 10th level, you can choose one damage type when you finish a short or long rest. You gain resistance to that damage type until you choose a different one with this feature. Damage from magical weapons or silver weapons ignores this resistance.\n\nNivel 10 - Fiendish Resilience\n\nPagina: 162\n\nChoose one damage type, other than Force, whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB. You have XPHB to that damage type until you choose a different one with this feature.\n\nNivel 10 - Fiendish Resilience\n\nNivel 14 - Hurl Through Hell\n\nPagina: 109\n\nStarting at 14th level, when you hit a creature with an attack, you can use this feature to instantly transport the target through the lower planes. The creature disappears and hurtles through a nightmare landscape.\n\nAt the end of your next turn, the target returns to the space it previously occupied, or the nearest unoccupied space. If the target is not a fiend, it takes 10d10 psychic damage as it reels from its horrific experience.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 14 - Hurl Through Hell\n\nPagina: 162\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with an attack roll, you can try to instantly transport the target through the Lower Planes. The target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC, or the target disappears and hurtles through a nightmare landscape. The target takes 8d10 Psychic damage if it isn't a Fiend, and it has the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn, when it returns to the space it previously occupied or the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 14 - Hurl Through Hell"},
  ["feature.fiend-patron.xphb2024.warlock.fiend.3"]={title="Fiend Patron",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 161\n\nMake a Deal with the Lower Planes\n\nYour pact draws on the Lower Planes, the realms of perdition. You might forge a bargain with a demon lord such as Demogorgon or Orcus; an archdevil such as Asmodeus; or a pit fiend, balor, yugoloth, or night hag that is especially mighty. That patron's aims are evil—the corruption or destruction of all things, ultimately including you—and your path is defined by the extent to which you strive against those aims."},
  ["feature.fiend-spells.xphb2024.warlock.fiend.3"]={title="Fiend Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 161\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Fiend Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.fiendish-auger.pabtso2014"]={title="Fiendish Auger",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 85 (9d12 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (can't see beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe auger deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe auger can burrow through solid rock at half its burrow speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFlaming Drill\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage. If the auger moves at least 20 feet in a straight line toward the target immediately before the hit, the target takes an additional 11 (2d10) piercing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBurst of Heat {@recharge 5}\n\nThe auger releases an intense burst of heat in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. This heat spreads around corners. Each creature in this area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 13 (3d8) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.fiendish-flesh-golem.bgdia2014"]={title="Fiendish Flesh Golem",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 236\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 210 (20d10 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 9 | CON 20 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBerserk\n\nWhenever the golem starts its turn with 100 hit points or fewer, roll a d6. On a 6, the golem goes berserk. On each of its turns while berserk, the golem attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, the golem attacks an object, with preference for an object smaller than itself. Once the golem goes berserk, it continues to do so until it is destroyed or regains all its hit points. If the golem's creator is within 60 feet of the berserk golem, the creator can try to calm it by speaking firmly and persuasively. The golem must be able to hear its creator, who must take an action to make a 15 Charisma (Persuasion) check. If the check succeeds, the golem ceases being berserk. If it takes damage while still at 100 hit points or fewer, the golem might go berserk again.\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever the golem is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe golem's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.fiendish-formian.coa2014"]={title="Fiendish Formian",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Formian\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: cold, fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHive Mind\n\nAll fiendish formians within 1 mile of Ekengarik can telepathically communicate with each other and Ekengarik.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe fiendish formian makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage and the target must make a 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target's Strength score is reduced by 1. The target dies if this reduces its Strength to 0. Otherwise, the reduction lasts until the target finishes a short or long rest."},
  ["creature.fiendish-giant-spider.oota2014"]={title="Fiendish Giant Spider",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned"},
  ["creature.fiendish-icon.abh2014"]={title="Fiendish Icon",subtitle="Criatura - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (5d6 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Infernal but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe icon has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe icon makes two Slam attacks and uses Fiery Eruption.\n\nSlam\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nFiery Eruption\n\ndex 11, each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the icon. actSaveFail 7 (2d6) Fire damage."},
  ["creature.fiendish-orc.crcotn2014"]={title="Fiendish Orc",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 71\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Orc\n\nImunidades: fire, poison"},
  ["feature.fiendish-resilience.phb2014.warlock.fiend.10"]={title="Fiendish Resilience",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 109\n\nStarting at 10th level, you can choose one damage type when you finish a short or long rest. You gain resistance to that damage type until you choose a different one with this feature. Damage from magical weapons or silver weapons ignores this resistance."},
  ["feature.fiendish-resilience.xphb2024.warlock.fiend.10"]={title="Fiendish Resilience",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.fiendish-spirit.tce2014"]={title="Fiendish Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe fiend has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nDeath Throes (Demon Only)\n\nWhen the fiend drops to 0 hit points or the spell ends, the fiend explodes, and each creature within 10 feet of it must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC. A creature takes 2d10 + summonSpellLevel fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nDevil's Sight (Devil Only)\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the fiend's darkvision.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe fiend makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (rounded down).\n\nBite (Demon Only)\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d12 + 3 + summonSpellLevel necrotic damage.\n\nClaws (Yugoloth Only)\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d8 + 3 + summonSpellLevel slashing damage. Immediately after the attack hits or misses, the fiend can magically teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nHurl Flame (Devil Only)\n\nrs hitYourSpellAttack to hit, range 150 ft., one target. h2d6 + 3 + summonSpellLevel fire damage. If the target is a flammable object that isn't being worn or carried, it also catches fire."},
  ["creature.fiendish-spirit.xphb2024"]={title="Fiendish Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 327\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, Telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes (Demon Only)\n\nWhen the spirit drops to 0 XPHB or the spell ends, the spirit explodes. dex DC equals your spell save DC, each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the spirit. actSaveFail 2d10 plus this spell's level Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nDevil's Sight (Devil Only)\n\nMagical XPHB doesn't impede the spirit's Darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe spirit has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spirit makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (round down).\n\nBite (Demon Only)\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d12 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Necrotic damage.\n\nClaws (Yugoloth Only)\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d8 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Slashing damage. Immediately after the attack hits or misses, the spirit can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nFiery Strike (Devil Only)\n\nm,r Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. or range 150 ft. h2d6 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Fire damage."},
  ["optionalfeature.fiendish-vigor.phb2014"]={title="Fiendish Vigor",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can cast false life on yourself at will as a 1st-level spell, without expending a spell slot or material components."},
  ["optionalfeature.fiendish-vigor.xphb2024"]={title="Fiendish Vigor",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nYou can cast XPHB on yourself without expending a spell slot. When you cast the spell with this feature, you don't roll the die for the XPHB; you automatically get the highest number on the die."},
  ["creature.fierna.coa2014"]={title="Fierna",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 225\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 367 (35d8 + 210)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 25 | CON 22 | INT 22 | WIS 22 | CHA 29\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: cold, fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nWhen a creature starts their turn within 120 feet of Fierna, they must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or have the frightened condition until they leave the aura. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to this effect for 1 hour.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nFierna regains 20 hit points at the start of her turn. If she takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of her next turn. Fierna dies only if she starts her turn with 0 hit points and is unable to regenerate.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Fierna fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nFierna has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nPrincess of Hellfire\n\nFire conjured by Fierna becomes Hellfire. It ignores resistances and immunities to fire damage, deals double damage to creatures vulnerable to fire or necrotic damage, can't be extinguished through any means, and is capable of melting stone or igniting inflammable objects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nFierna makes three attacks using Flame Blade, Mote of Flame, or a combination of the two.\n\nFlame Blade\n\nms 20 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h23 (4d6 + 9) fire damage.\n\nMote of Flame\n\nFierna targets a creature she can see within 90 feet of her. The target must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (3d8 + 9) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nWreath of Flames\n\nWhen hit by a melee attack and Fierna can see her attacker, she covers herself in Hellfire, and the attacker takes 13 (3d8) fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBlade\n\nFierna makes a Flame Blade attack.\n\nConjure Hellfire (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nFierna chooses a point she can see within 150 feet of her. All creatures in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nFierna summons an allied spined devil in an unoccupied space that she can see."},
  ["traphazard.fiery-blast-trap.xge2024"]={title="Fiery Blast Trap",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 113\n\nAnyone who steps on the mosaic causes fire to erupt from it. Those who openly wear holy symbols of Pyremius don't trigger this trap."},
  ["feature.fiery-soul.psk2014.sorcerer.pyromancer-psk.18"]={title="Fiery Soul",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nAt 18th level, you gain immunity to fire damage. In addition, any spell or effect you create ignores resistance to fire damage and treats immunity to fire damage as resistance to fire damage."},
  ["creature.figaro.veor2014"]={title="Figaro",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["class.fighter.phb2014"]={title="Fighter",subtitle="Classe - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\nFighting Style|Fighter||1\n\nSecond Wind|Fighter||1\n\nAction Surge|Fighter||2\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||4\n\nMartial Versatility|Fighter||4|TCE\n\nExtra Attack|Fighter||5\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||6\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||8\n\nIndomitable|Fighter||9\n\nExtra Attack (2)|Fighter||11\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||12\n\nIndomitable (two uses)|Fighter||13\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||14\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||16\n\nAction Surge (two uses)|Fighter||17\n\nIndomitable (three uses)|Fighter||17\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Fighter||19\n\nExtra Attack (3)|Fighter||20\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 72\n\nYou adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.\n\nNivel 1 - Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou have honed your martial prowess and gain a feats of your choice. XPHB is recommended.\n\nWhenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace the feat you chose with a different feats.\n\nNivel 1 - Fighting Style\n\nYou adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.\n\nNivel 1 - Second Wind\n\nPagina: 72\n\nYou have a limited well of stamina that you can draw on to protect yourself from harm. On your turn, you can use a bonus action to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + your fighter level.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again.\n\nNivel 1 - Second Wind\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou have a limited well of physical and mental stamina that you can draw on. As a XPHB, you can use it to regain XPHB equal to 1d10 plus your Fighter level.\n\nYou can use this feature twice. You regain one expended use when you finish a XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhen you reach certain Fighter levels, you gain more uses of this feature, as shown in the Second Wind column of the Fighter Features table.\n\nNivel 1 - Second Wind\n\nNivel 1 - Weapon Mastery\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYour training with weapons allows you to use the XPHB of three kinds of items or items weapons of your choice. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can practice weapon drills and change one of those weapon choices.\n\nWhen you reach certain Fighter levels, you gain the ability to use the XPHB of more kinds of weapons, as shown in the Weapon Mastery column of the Fighter Features table.\n\nNivel 2 - Action Surge\n\nPagina: 72\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again. Starting at 17th level, you can use it twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.\n\nNivel 2 - Action Surge\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action, except the XPHB action.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. Starting at level 17, you can use it twice before a rest but only once on a turn.\n\nNivel 2 - Action Surge\n\nNivel 2 - Tactical Mind\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou have a mind for tactics on and off the battlefield. When you fail an ability check, you can expend a use of your Second Wind to push yourself toward success. Rather than regaining XPHB, you roll 1d10 and add the number rolled to the ability check, potentially turning it into a success. If the check still fails, this use of Second Wind isn't expended.\n\nNivel 2 - Tactical Mind\n\nNivel 3 - Fighter Subclass\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a Fighter subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Fighter levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Fighter level or lower.\n\nNivel 3 - Martial Archetype\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 3rd level, you choose an archetype from the list available that you strive to emulate in your combat styles and techniques. The archetype you choose grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Fighter levels 6, 8, 12, 14, and 16.\n\nNivel 4 - Martial Versatility\n\nPagina: 41\n\n{@i 4th-level fighter tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, as you shift the focus of your martial practice:\n\n• Replace a optionalfeatures you know with another fighting style available to fighters.\n\n• If you know any optionalfeatures from the phb archetype, you can replace one maneuver you know with a different maneuver.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 72\n\nBeginning at 5th level, you can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nThe number of attacks increases to three when you reach 11th level in this class and to four when you reach 20th level in this class.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn.\n\nNivel 5 - Tactical Shift\n\nPagina: 92\n\nWhenever you activate your Second Wind with a XPHB, you can move up to half your XPHB without provoking XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 6th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 6 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 7 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 7th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 7 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 9 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 72\n\nBeginning at 9th level, you can reroll a saving throw that you fail. If you do so, you must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a long rest.\n\nYou can use this feature twice between long rests starting at 13th level and three times between long rests starting at 17th level.\n\nNivel 9 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 92\n\nIf you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level. You must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use this feature twice before a XPHB starting at level 13 and three times before a XPHB starting at level 17.\n\nNivel 9 - Indomitable\n\nNivel 9 - Tactical Master\n\nPagina: 92\n\nWhen you attack with a weapon whose mastery property you can use, you can replace that property with the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB property for that attack.\n\nNivel 9 - Tactical Master\n\nNivel 10 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 10 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 11 - Extra Attack (2)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 11th level, you can attack three times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Two Extra Attacks\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou can attack three times instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 13 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 92\n\nIf you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level. You must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use this feature twice before a XPHB starting at level 13 and three times before a XPHB starting at level 17.\n\nNivel 13 - Indomitable\n\nNivel 13 - Indomitable (two uses)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 13th level, you can use Indomitable twice between long rests.\n\nNivel 13 - Studied Attacks\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou study your opponents and learn from each attack you make. If you make an attack roll against a creature and miss, you have XPHB on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn.\n\nNivel 14 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 14th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 14 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 15 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 15th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 15 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 17 - Action Surge\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action, except the XPHB action.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. Starting at level 17, you can use it twice before a rest but only once on a turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Action Surge\n\nNivel 17 - Action Surge (two uses)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 17th level, you can use Action Surge twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 92\n\nIf you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level. You must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use this feature twice before a XPHB starting at level 13 and three times before a XPHB starting at level 17.\n\nNivel 17 - Indomitable\n\nNivel 17 - Indomitable (three uses)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 17th level, you can use Indomitable three times between long rests.\n\nNivel 18 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 18th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 18 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Extra Attack (3)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 20th level, you can attack four times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nNivel 20 - Three Extra Attacks\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou can attack four times instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn."},
  ["class.fighter.xphb2024"]={title="Fighter",subtitle="Classe - XPHB - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 72\n\nYou adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.\n\nNivel 1 - Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou have honed your martial prowess and gain a feats of your choice. XPHB is recommended.\n\nWhenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace the feat you chose with a different feats.\n\nNivel 1 - Fighting Style\n\nYou adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.\n\nNivel 1 - Second Wind\n\nPagina: 72\n\nYou have a limited well of stamina that you can draw on to protect yourself from harm. On your turn, you can use a bonus action to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + your fighter level.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again.\n\nNivel 1 - Second Wind\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou have a limited well of physical and mental stamina that you can draw on. As a XPHB, you can use it to regain XPHB equal to 1d10 plus your Fighter level.\n\nYou can use this feature twice. You regain one expended use when you finish a XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhen you reach certain Fighter levels, you gain more uses of this feature, as shown in the Second Wind column of the Fighter Features table.\n\nNivel 1 - Second Wind\n\nNivel 1 - Weapon Mastery\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYour training with weapons allows you to use the XPHB of three kinds of items or items weapons of your choice. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can practice weapon drills and change one of those weapon choices.\n\nWhen you reach certain Fighter levels, you gain the ability to use the XPHB of more kinds of weapons, as shown in the Weapon Mastery column of the Fighter Features table.\n\nNivel 2 - Action Surge\n\nPagina: 72\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you must finish a short or long rest before you can use it again. Starting at 17th level, you can use it twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.\n\nNivel 2 - Action Surge\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action, except the XPHB action.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. Starting at level 17, you can use it twice before a rest but only once on a turn.\n\nNivel 2 - Action Surge\n\nNivel 2 - Tactical Mind\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou have a mind for tactics on and off the battlefield. When you fail an ability check, you can expend a use of your Second Wind to push yourself toward success. Rather than regaining XPHB, you roll 1d10 and add the number rolled to the ability check, potentially turning it into a success. If the check still fails, this use of Second Wind isn't expended.\n\nNivel 2 - Tactical Mind\n\nNivel 3 - Fighter Subclass\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a Fighter subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Fighter levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Fighter level or lower.\n\nNivel 3 - Martial Archetype\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 3rd level, you choose an archetype from the list available that you strive to emulate in your combat styles and techniques. The archetype you choose grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Fighter levels 6, 8, 12, 14, and 16.\n\nNivel 4 - Martial Versatility\n\nPagina: 41\n\n{@i 4th-level fighter tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, as you shift the focus of your martial practice:\n\n• Replace a optionalfeatures you know with another fighting style available to fighters.\n\n• If you know any optionalfeatures from the phb archetype, you can replace one maneuver you know with a different maneuver.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 72\n\nBeginning at 5th level, you can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nThe number of attacks increases to three when you reach 11th level in this class and to four when you reach 20th level in this class.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn.\n\nNivel 5 - Tactical Shift\n\nPagina: 92\n\nWhenever you activate your Second Wind with a XPHB, you can move up to half your XPHB without provoking XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 6th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 6 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 7 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 7th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 7 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 9 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 72\n\nBeginning at 9th level, you can reroll a saving throw that you fail. If you do so, you must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a long rest.\n\nYou can use this feature twice between long rests starting at 13th level and three times between long rests starting at 17th level.\n\nNivel 9 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 92\n\nIf you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level. You must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use this feature twice before a XPHB starting at level 13 and three times before a XPHB starting at level 17.\n\nNivel 9 - Indomitable\n\nNivel 9 - Tactical Master\n\nPagina: 92\n\nWhen you attack with a weapon whose mastery property you can use, you can replace that property with the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB property for that attack.\n\nNivel 9 - Tactical Master\n\nNivel 10 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 10 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 11 - Extra Attack (2)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 11th level, you can attack three times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Two Extra Attacks\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou can attack three times instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 13 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 92\n\nIf you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level. You must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use this feature twice before a XPHB starting at level 13 and three times before a XPHB starting at level 17.\n\nNivel 13 - Indomitable\n\nNivel 13 - Indomitable (two uses)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 13th level, you can use Indomitable twice between long rests.\n\nNivel 13 - Studied Attacks\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou study your opponents and learn from each attack you make. If you make an attack roll against a creature and miss, you have XPHB on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn.\n\nNivel 14 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 14th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 14 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 15 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 15th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 15 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 17 - Action Surge\n\nPagina: 91\n\nYou can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action, except the XPHB action.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. Starting at level 17, you can use it twice before a rest but only once on a turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Action Surge\n\nNivel 17 - Action Surge (two uses)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 17th level, you can use Action Surge twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 92\n\nIf you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level. You must use the new roll, and you can't use this feature again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use this feature twice before a XPHB starting at level 13 and three times before a XPHB starting at level 17.\n\nNivel 17 - Indomitable\n\nNivel 17 - Indomitable (three uses)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 17th level, you can use Indomitable three times between long rests.\n\nNivel 18 - Martial Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 18th level, you gain a feature granted by your Martial Archetype.\n\nNivel 18 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain a feature from your Fighter Subclass.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 72\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Extra Attack (3)\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 20th level, you can attack four times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nNivel 20 - Three Extra Attacks\n\nPagina: 92\n\nYou can attack four times instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn."},
  ["feature.fighter-subclass.xphb2024.fighter.base.3"]={title="Fighter Subclass",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 92\n\nYou gain a Fighter subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Fighter levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Fighter level or lower."},
  ["feat.fighting-initiate.tce2014"]={title="Fighting Initiate",subtitle="Feat - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\nYour martial training has helped you develop a particular style of fighting. As a result, you learn one optionalfeatures option of your choice from the fighter class. If you already have a style, the one you choose must be different.\n\nWhenever you reach a level that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can replace this feat's fighting style with another one from the fighter class that you don't have."},
  ["feature.fighting-spirit.xge2024.fighter.samurai.3"]={title="Fighting Spirit",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 31\n\nStarting at 3rd level, your intensity in battle can shield you and help you strike true. As a bonus action on your turn, you can give yourself advantage on weapon attack rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain 5 temporary hit points. The number of temporary hit points increases when you reach certain levels in this class, increasing to 10 at 10th level and 15 at 15th level.\n\nYou can use this feature three times, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.phb2014.fighter.base.1"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.phb2014.paladin.base.2"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.phb2014.ranger.base.2"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.xge2024.bard.swords.3"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="At 3rd level, you adopt a style of fighting as your specialty. You can't take a Fighting Style option more than once, even if something in the game lets you choose again."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.xphb2024.fighter.base.1"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 91\n\nYou have honed your martial prowess and gain a feats of your choice. XPHB is recommended.\n\nWhenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace the feat you chose with a different feats."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.xphb2024.paladin.base.2"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="You gain a feats of your choice. Instead of choosing one of those feats, you can choose the XPHB Fighting Style."},
  ["feature.fighting-style.xphb2024.ranger.base.2"]={title="Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="You gain a feats of your choice. Instead of choosing one of those feats, you can choose the XPHB Fighting Style."},
  ["magicitem.figurine-of-wondrous-power-bronze-griffon.dmg2014"]={title="Figurine of Wondrous Power, Bronze Griffon",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA figurine of wondrous power is a statuette of a beast small enough to fit in a pocket. If you use an action to speak the command word and throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of you, the figurine becomes a living creature. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or if there isn't enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn't become a creature.\n\nThe creature is friendly to you and your companions. It understands your languages and obeys your spoken commands. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions.\n\nThe creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if it drops to 0 hit points or if you use an action to speak the command word again while touching it. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified in the figurine's description.\n\n{@creature griffon||Bronze Griffon}\n\nThis bronze statuette is of a griffon rampant. It can become a griffon for up to 6 hours. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed."},
  ["magicitem.figurine-of-wondrous-power-bronze-griffon.xdmg2024"]={title="Figurine of Wondrous Power, Bronze Griffon",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 261\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA XDMG is a statuette small enough to fit in a pocket. If you take a XPHB action to throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, the figurine becomes a living creature specified in the figurine's description below. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or if there isn't enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn't become a creature.\n\nThe creature is XPHB to you and your allies. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions.\n\nThe creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if its creature form drops to 0 XPHB or if you take a XPHB action while touching the creature to make it revert to figurine form. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified below.\n\nBronze Griffon (Rare)\n\nThis bronze statuette is of a griffon rampant. It can become a XMM for up to 6 hours. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed."},
  ["magicitem.figurine-of-wondrous-power-ebony-fly.dmg2014"]={title="Figurine of Wondrous Power, Ebony Fly",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA figurine of wondrous power is a statuette of a beast small enough to fit in a pocket. If you use an action to speak the command word and throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of you, the figurine becomes a living creature. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or if there isn't enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn't become a creature.\n\nThe creature is friendly to you and your companions. It understands your languages and obeys your spoken commands. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions.\n\nThe creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if it drops to 0 hit points or if you use an action to speak the command word again while touching it. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified in the figurine's description.\n\n{@creature giant fly|dmg|Ebony Fly}\n\nThis ebony statuette is carved in the likeness of a horsefly. It can become a dmg for up to 12 hours and can be ridden as a mount. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed."},
  ["magicitem.figurine-of-wondrous-power-ebony-fly.xdmg2024"]={title="Figurine of Wondrous Power, Ebony Fly",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 261\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA XDMG is a statuette small enough to fit in a pocket. If you take a XPHB action to throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, the figurine becomes a living creature specified in the figurine's description below. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or if there isn't enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn't become a creature.\n\nThe creature is XPHB to you and your allies. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions.\n\nThe creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if its creature form drops to 0 XPHB or if you take a XPHB action while touching the creature to make it revert to figurine form. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified below.\n\nEbony Fly (Rare)\n\nThis ebony statuette, carved in the likeness of a horsefly, can become a XDMG for up to 12 hours and can be ridden as a mount. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed."},
  ["magicitem.figurine-of-wondrous-power-golden-lions.dmg2014"]={title="Figurine of Wondrous Power, Golden Lions",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA figurine of wondrous power is a statuette of a beast small enough to fit in a pocket. If you use an action to speak the command word and throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of you, the figurine becomes a living creature. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or if there isn't enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn't become a creature.\n\nThe creature is friendly to you and your companions. It understands your languages and obeys your spoken commands. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions.\n\nThe creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if it drops to 0 hit points or if you use an action to speak the command word again while touching it. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified in the figurine's description.\n\n{@creature lion||Golden Lions}\n\nThese gold statuettes of lions are always created in pairs. You can use one figurine or both simultaneously. Each can become a lion for up to 1 hour. Once a lion has been used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed."},
  ["magicitem.figurine-of-wondrous-power-golden-lions.xdmg2024"]={title="Figurine of Wondrous Power, Golden Lions",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 261\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nA XDMG is a statuette small enough to fit in a pocket. If you take a XPHB action to throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, the figurine becomes a living creature specified in the figurine's description below. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or if there isn't enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn't become a creature.\n\nThe creature is XPHB to you and your allies. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions.\n\nThe creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if its creature form drops to 0 XPHB or if you take a XPHB action while touching the creature to make it revert to figurine form. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can't be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified below.\n\nGolden Lions (Rare)\n\nThese gold statuettes of lions are always created in pairs. You can use one figurine or both simultaneously. Each can become a XMM for up to 1 hour. Once a lion has been used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed."},
